{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YSUS4q9gw6L4vuHZvsHetZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — importance_margin_vla_compress\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: **CoRL 2026** (Austin, Nov 9-12; abstract May 26, paper May 29)\n5\t- Timeline: 6 days to abstract, 9 days to paper (as of 2026-05-20)\n6\t\n7\t## Title (working)\n8\t\"Why Token Pruning Crashes Some Robot Policies but Not Others: The Role of Vision Connectors in VLA Token Compressibility\"\n9\t\n10\t## Core Insight\n11\tVLA token compressibility is determined by the vision connector architecture. Evidence from **5 VLA models spanning 3 connector families** reveals a clean taxonomy:\n12\t- **Linear projection** (π0 3.3B): pruning-immune offline. π0 k=0.1 normalized loss = 0.976 (improves 2.4%). Tokens independently projected, information uniform.\n13\t- **Linear projection + deep post-processing** (X-VLA 880M, linear proj + 12-layer BART encoder): robust k≥0.9 (97.6% SR), **cliff at k=0.7 (56.2% SR, -43pp)**. BART encoder introduces non-linear mixing that creates partial token dependencies. CV=0.151 (between π0=0.038 and OpenVLA=0.215).\n14\t- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA 7B, OpenVLA-OFT 7B): graded degradation. k=0.1 normalized loss = 1.608 (+61%). Non-linear mixing creates partial dependencies. OFT entropy (0.667) ≈ Standard (0.661), confirming connector — not action head — determines attention structure.\n15\t- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA 450M): catastrophic cliff-edge. k=0.95 (removing 5%) → 0% SR. Spatial folding creates irreversible entanglement.\n16\t\n17\tKey controlled comparison: π0 (256 tokens, linear) vs OpenVLA (256 tokens, 3-layer MLP) — same token count, same encoder lineage, only connector differs. k=0.1: π0 improves 2.4% vs OpenVLA degrades 61%. This isolates connector as the causal factor.\n18\t\n19\tLearned re-encoding (VTR) overcomes the cliff-edge: cross-attention 60.1±1.3% and MLP adapter 63.4±2.6% at M=32 (vs 0% hard pruning), with M=128 passthrough (58.0%±3.5, 3-seed) confirming the gain comes from re-encoding itself, not compression. SmolVLA M-curve confirmed flat (D105): M=16 (56.9%±1.3) = M=128 (58.0%±3.5), all 5 M-values within ±5pp. VTR achieves near-lossless compression at any ratio for pixel-shuffle connectors.\n20\t\n21\t## Paper Identity (Round 4 Upgrade, 2026-05-20)\n22\t**ANALYSIS + METHOD paper.** (D091 → D097: expanded from 2-3 models to 5 models across 3 connector families)\n23\t\n24\t**Analysis contribution (primary)**: First systematic study of why token pruning catastrophically fails on some VLA architectures. We show that the effective vision-to-LLM projection pipeline determines pruning robustness along a continuous spectrum (CV: 0.038→0.314): pure linear projection is immune, linear+deep post-processing shows a cliff pattern, MLP projectors degrade smoothly, and pixel-shuffle collapses catastrophically. 5 models across 4 model sizes (450M-7B) eliminate size confound. No competing work does cross-architecture VLA token analysis.\n25\t\n26\t**Method contribution**: Diagnose-then-Compress framework:\n27\t- Step 1: **Connector Compressibility Diagnostic** (D104: resolved)\n28\t  - **Primary metric: Importance CV** (token importance heterogeneity) — zero-cost, one forward pass\n29\t  - CV forms continuous spectrum predicting pruning tolerance: π0=0.038 < X-VLA=0.151 < OpenVLA=0.215 < SmolVLA=0.314\n30\t  - ⚠️ D106+: X-VLA CV=0.151 correctly predicted its intermediate pruning behavior (k=0.7 ≈50% SR ≈ OpenVLA k=0.7). CV is a valid continuous predictor, NOT a 3-class discrete classifier.\n31\t  - **Key discovery**: X-VLA \"linear projection\" passes through BART encoder (12 transformer layers) before decoder → introduces non-linear mixing → explains CV=0.151 (much higher than π0=0.038 pure linear)\n32\t  - **Entropy as mechanistic supplement**:\n33\t    - π0: entropy=0.959 (per-layer mean, range 0.931–0.983), CV=0.038 — uniform & independent → most tolerant\n34\t    - X-VLA: entropy=0.614, CV=0.151 — selective & BART-mixed → intermediate\n35\t    - OpenVLA: entropy=0.661, CV=0.215 — selective & MLP-mixed → graded\n36\t    - SmolVLA: entropy=0.952, CV=0.314 — near-uniform but spatially entangled → catastrophic\n37\t  - NOTE: X-VLA entropy=0.614 (NOT \"high\"), similar to OpenVLA 0.661. Both go through non-linear mixing.\n38\t  - ✅ Batch 2 complete: continuous CV spectrum confirmed (X-VLA full 8-point curve validates threshold-graded class)\n39\t  - Supplementary: lightweight pruning probe (remove 5%, one forward pass) as practitioner-friendly alternative\n40\t- Step 2: VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) — lightweight cross-attention module (~22M params) for universal compression\n41\t- For entangled tokens (pixel-shuffle): recovers from 0% to 60%+, M-curve confirmed flat D105 (near-lossless at any compression ratio)\n42\t- For independent tokens (MLP projector): **D109 C4-ext confirmed 0% SR** at 20K steps (M=128, severe overfitting — model outputs identical action every step). VTR on MLP projector does NOT improve SR; reframed as \"VTR ceiling depends on connector type\" finding. User directive: performance degradation acceptable if efficiency improves — VTR value is 75% KV-cache reduction + attention speedup. VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress to test whether smaller M values fare better.\n43\t\n44\t**Differentiation from concurrent work**: 4 concurrent works (Compressor-VLA, SpecPrune-VLA, LightVLA ICRA'26, See What Matters ICML'26) all propose pruning on MLP-projector VLAs. We (1) explain why pruning fails on pixel-shuffle architectures, (2) identify why pruning succeeds on linear projection (tokens are truly independent), and (3) propose a re-encoding method motivated by the diagnostic analysis.\n45\t\n46\t**Model coverage**: 5 VLA models × 3 connector families × 4 model sizes (450M-7B). RC1 (only 2 models) and RC2 (size confound) fully addressed.\n47\t\n48\t## Core Claims (5 claims, expanded from 4)\n49\t\n50\t### Claim 1: Architecture-Dependent Compressibility (taxonomy — D107 RESOLVED)\n51\tThe effective vision-to-LLM projection pipeline determines pruning robustness. Evidence from 5 VLA models:\n52\t- **Pure linear projection** (π0): immune — k=0.1 loss improves 2.4%\n53\t- **Linear + deep post-processing** (X-VLA, BART 12L): **threshold-graded** — immune k≥0.9 (97.6%), threshold at k=0.7 (56.2%, -43pp), then graded degradation k≤0.5 (42.6%→23.0%→~4%→~0%). Distinct from SmolVLA's catastrophic cliff (any pruning → 0%)\n54\t- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA, OFT): smooth graded degradation. k=0.5 → 37.4% (-49% relative)\n55\t- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA): **catastrophic cliff** — k=0.95 (5% removal) → 0% SR. Any pruning destroys.\n56\t- **CV predicts degradation onset**: 0.038 (immune) → 0.151 (threshold-graded at k=0.7) → 0.215 (immediate onset) → 0.314 (catastrophic cliff)\n57\t\n58\t**Evidence**: 5 models, 3 connector families, 4 model sizes (450M-7B). Key controlled comparison: π0 (256 tokens, linear) k=0.1 = 0.976 vs OpenVLA (256 tokens, 3-layer MLP) k=0.1 = 1.608. Same token count, same encoder lineage, only connector differs. X-VLA cliff pattern (k=0.9: 97.6% → k=0.7: 56.2%) confirms intermediate CV predicts intermediate behavior.\n59\t\n60\t⚠️ **D108: Pruning method discrepancy** — Offline diagnostic uses L2_norm_zero_out (all models). But LIBERO closed-loop evals differ: OpenVLA = random removal (torch.randperm, physical), X-VLA = L2 norm removal (importance-based, physical). SmolVLA = all methods tested (all 0%). This STRENGTHENS findings (OpenVLA survives even random = hardest test; X-VLA cliffs even with importance-based = easiest test), but paper must accurately report. OpenVLA L2 norm comparison experiment planned for fair cross-model comparison.\n61\t\n62\t### Claim 2: Pixel Shuffle Creates Irreversible Token Entanglement\n63\tSmolVLA's pixel_shuffle connector spatially folds 1024 SigLIP patches into 64 tokens per camera (16x compression). Each resulting token encodes a 32x32 pixel region via channel-to-spatial reorganization. This creates extreme cross-token spatial entanglement: removing any single token eliminates an entire spatial quadrant's information with no redundancy to compensate.\n64\t\n65\t**Evidence**:\n66\t- k=0.95 (remove only 7/128 tokens = 5.5%) = 0% SR — even minimal removal is catastrophic\n67\t- k=0.9 (remove 13/128 tokens) = 0% SR\n68\t- Geometric prior (Sobel edge) k=0.5/0.7/0.9 = all 0%\n69\t- Attention entropy ratio 0.952 (near-uniform, TV=0.05)\n70\t- Official checkpoint Object (59.2% baseline) cliff-edge at k=0.5 → 0%\n71\t- Official checkpoint Spatial (43.8% baseline) cliff-edge at k=0.5 → 0.6% (3/500, CI [0.2%, 1.7%])\n72\t\n73\t### Claim 3a: Linear Projection → Depends on Effective Pipeline (D107: RESOLVED)\n74\tPure linear projection (π0): immune. Linear projection + deep post-processing (X-VLA, BART 12L): \"robust-then-cliff\" — immune at k≥0.9, cliff at k=0.7, then graded degradation. The BART encoder introduces non-linear cross-token mixing that explains intermediate CV=0.151 and the cliff pattern.\n75\t\n76\t**Evidence** (X-VLA LIBERO SR — Batch 1 + Batch 2 COMPLETE, full 8-point curve):\n77\t- k=1.0: **99.2%** (baseline, 496/500) — per-task: [98, 100, 98, 100, 100, 96, 100, 100, 100, 100]\n78\t- k=0.95: **99.0%** (-0.2pp) — per-task: [98, 100, 100, 96, 100, 96, 100, 100, 100, 100]\n79\t- k=0.9: **97.6%** (-1.6pp) — per-task: [96, 98, 100, 92, 100, 96, 100, 98, 96, 100]\n80\t- k=0.7: **56.2%** (-43pp, CLIFF — 281/500) — per-task: [94, 2, 100, 80, 28, 92, 12, 66, 0, 88]\n81\t- k=0.5: **42.6%** (-57pp) — Batch 2 confirmed (MSH fix applied)\n82\t- k=0.3: **23.0%** (-77pp) — graded degradation continues below cliff\n83\t- k=0.2: **~4.0%** (-96pp) — near-zero\n84\t- k=0.1: **~0.0%** (-100pp) — complete failure\n85\t✅ Full curve confirms threshold-graded pattern: immune k≥0.9, cliff at k=0.7, then graded degradation k≤0.5 (42.6%→23.0%→~4%→~0%).\n86\t\n87\tπ0 evidence:\n88\t- π0 (3.3B, 256 tokens, pure linear proj): k=0.1 normalized_L1 = 0.976 (-2.4% = improvement), k=0.5 = 0.983\n89\t- Attention entropy: π0 suffix-to-vision mean 0.959 (near-uniform across 18 layers, range [0.931, 0.983])\n90\t- Importance CV: π0 = 0.038 (lowest in spectrum)\n91\t\n92\t**Key insight**: \"Linear projection\" is NOT sufficient for immunity. The effective pipeline matters. X-VLA's BART encoder (12 transformer layers after linear proj) introduces partial dependencies → CV=0.151 → cliff at k=0.7. π0's pure linear proj → CV=0.038 → immune even at k=0.1.\n93\t\n94\t### Claim 3b: MLP Projector → Graded Degradation\n95\tMulti-layer MLP connectors create partial token dependencies through non-linear mixing, enabling graceful but real degradation.\n96\t\n97\t**Evidence** (OpenVLA 6-point degradation curve):\n98\t- k=1.0: 74.0% (baseline)\n99\t- k=0.95: 69.4% (-6% relative)\n100\t- k=0.9: 62.0% (-16% relative)\n101\t- k=0.7: 49.0% (-34% relative)\n102\t- k=0.5: 37.4% (-49% relative)\n103\t- k=0.3: 20.6% (-72% relative)\n104\t- Entropy ratio 0.639 (progressive sharpening L0=0.98→L29=0.48, TV=0.50)\n105\t- OFT (same connector, different action head): entropy 0.667 ≈ Standard 0.661 → connector determines attention structure, not action head\n106\t- CogACT (MLP projector, literature): 74.8% → 74.2% under 78% pruning (EfficientVLA)\n107\t\n108\t### Claim 4: Learned Re-Encoding Overcomes Cliff-Edge Where Deletion Fails (D072+MLP confirmed → upgraded to METHOD per D091)\n109\tTwo independent re-encoding architectures (~22M params each) validate that **any learned re-encoding** can transform entangled pixel_shuffle tokens into effective representations. **The core mechanism is re-encoding itself, not the specific architecture**: cross-attention (60.1±1.3%, 3-seed) and MLP adapter (63.4±2.6%, 3-seed) both recover from 0% hard pruning, with p≈0.15 confirming no significant difference. M=128 passthrough (~60.0%, 2-seed) achieves +15pp over baseline 44.8%, proving the gain comes from re-encoding rather than compression. M=64 achieves best tradeoff at 62.0±2.3% with 50% compression. Cross-suite generalization confirmed: M=32 recovers to 53.2% on Spatial (vs 0.6% pruning cliff-edge) and 56.4% on Goal. M=96 dip statistically confirmed (p=0.034 vs M=64).\n110\t\n111\t**D109 C4-ext on OpenVLA (MLP projector)**: M=128 VTR at 20K steps = **0% SR** (severe overfitting, model outputs identical action every step). This suggests VTR's effectiveness is connector-dependent: pixel-shuffle benefits enormously (0%→60%+) because re-encoding repairs spatial entanglement, while MLP projector tokens are already individually meaningful and VTR adds unnecessary complexity. VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress — if these also fail, VTR is specifically a pixel-shuffle solution, which strengthens the architecture-dependency narrative.\n112\t\n113\t**Evidence** (all confirmed):\n114\t\n115\tCross-attention re-encoding (M sweep, 3-seed where available):\n116\t| M | Compression | SR (3-seed mean±std) | Seeds | Notes |\n117\t|---|------------|-----|-----|-----|\n118\t| 16 | 87.5% | **56.9±1.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ ZERO loss vs M=128 |\n119\t| 32 | 75% | **60.1±1.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ |\n120\t| 64 | 50% | **62.0±2.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ best tradeoff |\n121\t| 96 | 25% | 54.5±3.2% | 42/43/44 | ✅ highest variance |\n122\t| 128 | 0% (passthrough) | **58.0±3.5%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ passthrough control |\n123\t\n124\tMLP adapter control (M=32, ~22.14M params, 3-seed):\n125\t| Architecture | Params | M | Mean SR (3-seed) | Std | Individual seeds |\n126\t|---|---|---|-----|-----|-----|\n127\t| Cross-attention (VTC) | 22.2M | 32 | **60.1%** | ±1.3 | 61.6 / 59.2 / 59.6 |\n128\t| **MLP adapter** | **22.14M** | **32** | **63.4%** | **±2.6** | **65.2 / 64.6 / 60.4** |\n129\t\n130\tTwo-sample t-test: t≈1.94, p≈0.15 → **no significant difference** (α=0.05). Both >> 0% (hard pruning) and > 44.8% (baseline). MLP ≥ VTC in all 3 seeds but difference not statistically significant — confirms re-encoding mechanism, not architecture, is the causal factor. (Note: M=32 seed43 corrected from 62.4% to 59.2% per registry verification; 62.4% was M=96 seed43 CI upper bound misattributed.)\n131\t\n132\t## Story Spine\n133\t\n134\t**Problem**: Vision token efficiency is critical for real-time VLA deployment. Growing literature proposes inference-time token reduction (FastV, VLA-IAP, H2O, ToMe). These methods succeed on some VLAs but their behavior across different architectures is unstudied.\n135\t\n136\t**Gap**: No work has systematically compared token pruning robustness across VLA architectures. The implicit assumption that \"token pruning works or fails uniformly\" is untested. The critical architectural factor determining prunability is unknown.\n137\t\n138\t**Discovery**: We find that the effective vision-to-LLM projection pipeline determines token pruning robustness. Testing 5 VLA models (450M-7B):\n139\t- **Pure linear projection** (π0): immune. k=0.1 loss improves 2.4%.\n140\t- **Linear + deep post-processing** (X-VLA, BART 12L): threshold-graded — robust k≥0.9, threshold at k=0.7 (97.6%→56.2%), then graded below.\n141\t- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA, OFT): smooth graded degradation. k=0.5 → 37.4% (-49%).\n142\t- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA): catastrophic cliff. k=0.95 → 0% SR.\n143\tCV of token importance (0.038→0.151→0.215→0.314) is a continuous predictor: lower CV = later onset of degradation.\n144\t\n145\t**Solution**: Diagnose-then-Compress framework. Step 1: Token importance CV provides zero-cost diagnostic for pruning tolerance (one forward pass). Step 2: VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) provides universal compression. For pixel-shuffle: recovers from 0% to 60%+ SR, M-curve confirmed flat (D105: M=16 56.9% ≈ M=128 58.0%, near-lossless at any compression ratio). For MLP projector: D109 C4-ext = 0% SR (overfitting at M=128); VTC-only M=32/M=64 in progress.\n146\t\n147\t**Headline result**: \"Across 5 VLA models spanning 3 connector architectures, we find that pruning tolerance depends on the effective vision-to-LLM pipeline: pure linear projection is immune (π0: loss improves 2.4% at 90% removal), linear projection with deep post-processing shows a cliff pattern (X-VLA: 97.6% at k=0.9, 56.2% at k=0.7), MLP connectors degrade smoothly (OpenVLA: -49% at 50% removal), and pixel-shuffle collapses catastrophically (SmolVLA: 0% at 5% removal). Token importance CV predicts this spectrum. For vulnerable architectures, VTR achieves 60%+ SR at 75% compression where deletion achieves 0%.\"\n148\t\n149\t## Paper Structure (5-model version)\n150\t\n151\t1. **Introduction**: VLA efficiency motivation → diverse connector architectures → 4-class taxonomy discovery → Diagnose-then-Compress framework\n152\t2. **Background**: 5 VLA models, 3 connector families (linear/MLP/pixel-shuffle), token flow analysis\n153\t3. **Experimental Setup**: 5 models, LIBERO benchmark, pruning protocol, VTR compression, diagnostic metrics\n154\t4. **Main Results**:\n155\t   - §4.1: 4-Class Taxonomy Overview (Table 1: 5 models × pruning sensitivity)\n156\t   - §4.2: Catastrophic — pixel-shuffle cliff-edge (SmolVLA, all configs 0%)\n157\t   - §4.3: Graded — MLP degradation (OpenVLA 6-point curve + OFT entropy confirmation)\n158\t   - §4.4: Immune — linear projection (π0 + X-VLA, controlled comparison with OpenVLA)\n159\t   - §4.5: VTR overcomes cliff-edge (M-curve flat + architecture independence)\n160\t5. **Analysis**:\n161\t   - §5.1: Why pixel_shuffle creates entanglement (spatial folding + controlled comparison)\n162\t   - §5.2: Diagnostic metric — Entropy + CV composite (D104, 4-model validation)\n163\t   - §5.3: Re-encoding mechanism (M=128 passthrough + MLP adapter + M-curve flat D105)\n164\t6. **Discussion**: Design implications, limitations (LIBERO only, no real robot), future work\n165\t7. **Conclusion**: 5 claims summary\n166\t\n167\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n168\t\n169\t### RC1: Only 2 models → **FULLY ADDRESSED**\n170\t**Response**: Now 5 models (SmolVLA, OpenVLA, OpenVLA-OFT, π0, X-VLA) across 3 connector families (pixel-shuffle, 3-layer MLP, linear projection) and 4 model sizes (450M-7B). Each connector class has ≥2 models.\n171\t\n172\t### RC2: Model size confound (450M vs 7B) → **FULLY ADDRESSED**\n173\t**Response**: π0 (3.3B, linear) is pruning-immune while OpenVLA (7B, MLP) degrades 61% at k=0.1. Larger model is MORE vulnerable, not less — directly falsifies \"larger models are more robust\" hypothesis. X-VLA (880M, linear) also immune, matching π0 behavior despite 4× smaller. Size is not the explanatory variable; connector type is.\n174\t\n175\t### RC3: Why not test SmolVLA without pixel_shuffle?\n176\t**Response**: SmolVLA's connector is integral (LLM expects 128 tokens, not 1024). Removing it requires retraining from scratch. OpenVLA comparison isolates the connector's role.\n177\t\n178\t### RC4: Smart compression — is re-encoding or compression the mechanism?\n179\t**Response**: Two independent lines of evidence. (1) M=128 passthrough control: M=128 (no compression) = 59.8% vs M=32 (75% compression) = 61.6%. The +15pp over baseline comes from re-encoding; compression is a free bonus. (2) Architecture control: MLP adapter (65.2%) ≈ cross-attention (61.6%) with CI overlap — re-encoding works regardless of the specific mechanism. Both lines converge: the causal factor is learned re-encoding, not cross-attention specifically nor compression.\n180\t\n181\t### RC5: Relationship to VLA-IAP\n182\t**Response**: VLA-IAP's 97.8% on OpenVLA is consistent with our finding: MLP projector preserves token independence. VLA-IAP untested on pixel_shuffle VLAs; our geometric prior experiments (0%) predict it would fail.\n183\t\n184\t### RC6: Is this just \"different models behave differently\"?\n185\t**Response**: We identify the specific mechanism (pixel_shuffle spatial folding) and provide evidence for WHY. Concrete design implications: future VLAs wanting efficiency should avoid pixel_shuffle or include learned re-encoding modules.\n186\t\n187\t## All Experimental Evidence (confirmed)\n188\t\n189\t### SmolVLA Cliff-Edge\n190\t- Fine-tuned baseline (Object): 44.8% (224/500)\n191\t- 6 pruning conditions (random/ACIS/ToMe × k=0.5/0.7/0.9): all 0%\n192\t- Geometric prior (Sobel) k=0.5/0.7/0.9: all 0%\n193\t- Attention entropy: 0.952 (flat, TV=0.05)\n194\t- Official checkpoint Object: 59.2% → 0% at k=0.5\n195\t- Official checkpoint Spatial: 43.8% → 0.6% (3/500, CI [0.2%, 1.7%]) at k=0.5 — near-zero, confirms cliff-edge across suites\n196\t\n197\t### OpenVLA Degradation Curve\n198\t- k=1.0: 74.0% (370/500)\n199\t- k=0.95: 69.4% (-6% relative)\n200\t- k=0.9: 62.0% (-16% relative)\n201\t- k=0.7: 49.0% (245/500, -34% relative)\n202\t- k=0.5: 37.4% (187/500, -49% relative)\n203\t- k=0.3: 20.6% (103/500, -72% relative)\n204\t- Entropy: 0.639 (progressive sharpening, TV=0.50)\n205\t\n206\t### Cross-Model Pruning Taxonomy (NEW — D100 confirmed all L2_norm_zero_out)\n207\t| Model | Connector | Tokens | k=0.1 norm_L1 | k=0.5 norm_L1 | Class |\n208\t|-------|-----------|--------|---------------|---------------|-------|\n209\t| π0 (3.3B) | Pure linear proj | 256 | 0.976 (-2.4%) | 0.983 | Immune |\n210\t| X-VLA (880M) | Linear + BART 12L | 50 | ~1.00 | ~1.00 | Threshold-graded (k=0.7: 56.2%) |\n211\t| OpenVLA (7B) | 3-layer MLP | 256 | 1.608 (+61%) | 1.167 (+17%) | Smooth graded |\n212\t| OFT (7B) | 3-layer MLP | 256 | pending (M031) | — | (entropy=0.667≈Std) |\n213\t| SmolVLA (450M) | Pixel-shuffle | 128 | — | 0% cliff | Catastrophic |\n214\t\n215\tDiagnostic metrics (D104+D106: CV as continuous predictor):\n216\t| Model | Connector (effective) | Entropy | CV | Pruning Behavior |\n217\t|-------|----------------------|---------|------|------------------|\n218\t| π0 | Pure linear proj | 0.959 | 0.038 | Immune (offline, k=0.1 improves) |\n219\t| X-VLA | Linear proj + BART enc (12L) | **0.614** | **0.151** | Threshold-graded: robust k≥0.9, cliff k=0.7 (56.2%) |\n220\t| OpenVLA | 3-layer MLP (GELU) | 0.661 | 0.215 | Graded (74→37.4% at k=0.5) |\n221\t| OFT | 3-layer MLP (GELU) | 0.667 | — | (entropy≈Standard, confirms connector) |\n222\t| SmolVLA | Pixel-shuffle (16×) | 0.952 | **0.314** | Catastrophic (0% at k=0.95) |\n223\t\n224\tKey insights (updated with X-VLA data):\n225\t1. **CV is a continuous predictor**: 0.038 → 0.151 → 0.215 → 0.314 maps to decreasing pruning tolerance. NOT a 3-class discrete classifier.\n226\t2. **X-VLA CV=0.151 correctly predicted its intermediate behavior** — closer to OpenVLA (0.215) than π0 (0.038), matching k=0.7 SR ≈ OpenVLA k=0.7.\n227\t3. **X-VLA entropy=0.614 ≈ OpenVLA 0.661** — both have BART/MLP non-linear mixing. X-VLA is NOT \"high entropy\" like π0.\n228\t4. **Effective connector complexity matters more than nominal label**: X-VLA is \"linear proj\" but BART encoder introduces 12 transformer layers of mixing. Paper should discuss \"effective connector\" = projection + any intermediate processing.\n229\t5. OFT entropy 0.667 ≈ Standard 0.661 → action head does not affect attention structure\n230\t6. Framing: CV captures \"degree of non-linear mixing in the vision-to-LLM pathway.\" More mixing → higher CV → less tolerant of pruning.\n231\t\n232\t### Smart Compress (Learned Re-encoding)\n233\tCross-attention (VTC) M sweep (3-seed where available):\n234\t- M=16: **56.9% ± 1.3pp** (3-seed: 55.8/58.4/56.5) — 87.5% compression, ZERO loss vs M=128\n235\t- M=32: 60.1±1.3% (3-seed: 61.6/59.2/59.6)\n236\t- M=64: 62.0±2.3% (3-seed: 61.6/60.0/64.4)\n237\t- M=96: 54.5±3.2% (3-seed: 52.6/58.2/52.8) — highest variance\n238\t- M=128: 58.0±3.5pp (3-seed: 59.8/54.0/60.2) — passthrough control\n239\t- **D102 CONFIRMED: M-curve is flat.** M=16 (56.9%) = M=128 (58.0%), difference < 1.1pp. VTC achieves near-lossless compression at ANY ratio for pixel-shuffle connector. All M values within ±5pp of baseline ~59%.\n240\t\n241\tMLP adapter (M=32, 3-seed):\n242\t- seed42: 65.2% (326/500), seed43: 64.6% (323/500), seed44: 60.4% (302/500)\n243\t- Mean: 63.4% ± 2.6 vs VTC M=32 mean 60.1% ± 1.3\n244\t- t-test p≈0.15, no significant difference — confirms architecture-independence\n245\t\n246\t### D109: VTR on OpenVLA (MLP projector) — FAILED\n247\t- C4-ext M=128 at 20K steps: **0% SR** (0/44 episodes before eval termination)\n248\t- Failure mode: model outputs identical action every timestep (severe overfitting)\n249\t- Interpretation: VTR adds unnecessary complexity for MLP projector tokens (already individually meaningful). VTR specifically solves pixel-shuffle entanglement.\n250\t- VTC-only M=32 and M=64 training in progress on westd-41074:2-3\n251\t\n252\t### Cross-Suite VTR Generalization (SmolVLA)\n253\t- M=32 Spatial: 53.2% (vs official Spatial baseline 43.8%, vs pruning 0.6% — recovery from cliff-edge AND exceeds uncompressed baseline)\n254\t- M=32 Goal: 56.4% (vs official Goal baseline 63.0%, vs pruning 0% — recovery from cliff-edge but below uncompressed baseline; frame as compression-recovery, not performance boost)\n255\t- Note: VTR trained on Object suite, evaluated cross-suite. Official baselines from different checkpoint (official vs LoRA-FT); comparisons should emphasize recovery from 0% rather than absolute performance vs uncompressed.\n256\t\n257\t### Pairwise Statistical Tests (Welch's t-test, n=3 per condition)\n258\t- M=32 VTC vs M=32 MLP: p=0.150 (not significant) — confirms architecture-independence\n259\t- M=64 VTC vs M=96 VTC: p=0.034 (significant) — M=96 dip confirmed real\n260\t- M=32 MLP vs M=96 VTC: p=0.022 (significant) — M=96 underperforms\n261\t- M=32/M=64/M=128 VTC cluster: all pairwise p>0.25 — robust across M values\n262\t- Bonferroni note: no pair survives correction at 10 tests; n=3 limits power (~0.2 for medium effects)\n263\t\n264\t### Supplementary\n265\t- Inference latency: 6% speedup at M=32\n266\t- KV-cache: 75% memory reduction at M=32\n267\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb0141ba-9b41-4c32-a6f9-94e34c15fbb4","uuid":"6206032b-9464-4387-8bb8-95fe6914551c","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:28:05.312Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T155932/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — importance_margin_vla_compress\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: **CoRL 2026** (Austin, Nov 9-12; abstract May 26, paper May 29)\n- Timeline: 6 days to abstract, 9 days to paper (as of 2026-05-20)\n\n## Title (working)\n\"Why Token Pruning Crashes Some Robot Policies but Not Others: The Role of Vision Connectors in VLA Token Compressibility\"\n\n## Core Insight\nVLA token compressibility is determined by the vision connector architecture. Evidence from **5 VLA models spanning 3 connector families** reveals a clean taxonomy:\n- **Linear projection** (π0 3.3B): pruning-immune offline. π0 k=0.1 normalized loss = 0.976 (improves 2.4%). Tokens independently projected, information uniform.\n- **Linear projection + deep post-processing** (X-VLA 880M, linear proj + 12-layer BART encoder): robust k≥0.9 (97.6% SR), **cliff at k=0.7 (56.2% SR, -43pp)**. BART encoder introduces non-linear mixing that creates partial token dependencies. CV=0.151 (between π0=0.038 and OpenVLA=0.215).\n- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA 7B, OpenVLA-OFT 7B): graded degradation. k=0.1 normalized loss = 1.608 (+61%). Non-linear mixing creates partial dependencies. OFT entropy (0.667) ≈ Standard (0.661), confirming connector — not action head — determines attention structure.\n- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA 450M): catastrophic cliff-edge. k=0.95 (removing 5%) → 0% SR. Spatial folding creates irreversible entanglement.\n\nKey controlled comparison: π0 (256 tokens, linear) vs OpenVLA (256 tokens, 3-layer MLP) — same token count, same encoder lineage, only connector differs. k=0.1: π0 improves 2.4% vs OpenVLA degrades 61%. This isolates connector as the causal factor.\n\nLearned re-encoding (VTR) overcomes the cliff-edge: cross-attention 60.1±1.3% and MLP adapter 63.4±2.6% at M=32 (vs 0% hard pruning), with M=128 passthrough (58.0%±3.5, 3-seed) confirming the gain comes from re-encoding itself, not compression. SmolVLA M-curve confirmed flat (D105): M=16 (56.9%±1.3) = M=128 (58.0%±3.5), all 5 M-values within ±5pp. VTR achieves near-lossless compression at any ratio for pixel-shuffle connectors.\n\n## Paper Identity (Round 4 Upgrade, 2026-05-20)\n**ANALYSIS + METHOD paper.** (D091 → D097: expanded from 2-3 models to 5 models across 3 connector families)\n\n**Analysis contribution (primary)**: First systematic study of why token pruning catastrophically fails on some VLA architectures. We show that the effective vision-to-LLM projection pipeline determines pruning robustness along a continuous spectrum (CV: 0.038→0.314): pure linear projection is immune, linear+deep post-processing shows a cliff pattern, MLP projectors degrade smoothly, and pixel-shuffle collapses catastrophically. 5 models across 4 model sizes (450M-7B) eliminate size confound. No competing work does cross-architecture VLA token analysis.\n\n**Method contribution**: Diagnose-then-Compress framework:\n- Step 1: **Connector Compressibility Diagnostic** (D104: resolved)\n  - **Primary metric: Importance CV** (token importance heterogeneity) — zero-cost, one forward pass\n  - CV forms continuous spectrum predicting pruning tolerance: π0=0.038 < X-VLA=0.151 < OpenVLA=0.215 < SmolVLA=0.314\n  - ⚠️ D106+: X-VLA CV=0.151 correctly predicted its intermediate pruning behavior (k=0.7 ≈50% SR ≈ OpenVLA k=0.7). CV is a valid continuous predictor, NOT a 3-class discrete classifier.\n  - **Key discovery**: X-VLA \"linear projection\" passes through BART encoder (12 transformer layers) before decoder → introduces non-linear mixing → explains CV=0.151 (much higher than π0=0.038 pure linear)\n  - **Entropy as mechanistic supplement**:\n    - π0: entropy=0.959 (per-layer mean, range 0.931–0.983), CV=0.038 — uniform & independent → most tolerant\n    - X-VLA: entropy=0.614, CV=0.151 — selective & BART-mixed → intermediate\n    - OpenVLA: entropy=0.661, CV=0.215 — selective & MLP-mixed → graded\n    - SmolVLA: entropy=0.952, CV=0.314 — near-uniform but spatially entangled → catastrophic\n  - NOTE: X-VLA entropy=0.614 (NOT \"high\"), similar to OpenVLA 0.661. Both go through non-linear mixing.\n  - ✅ Batch 2 complete: continuous CV spectrum confirmed (X-VLA full 8-point curve validates threshold-graded class)\n  - Supplementary: lightweight pruning probe (remove 5%, one forward pass) as practitioner-friendly alternative\n- Step 2: VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) — lightweight cross-attention module (~22M params) for universal compression\n- For entangled tokens (pixel-shuffle): recovers from 0% to 60%+, M-curve confirmed flat D105 (near-lossless at any compression ratio)\n- For independent tokens (MLP projector): **D109 C4-ext confirmed 0% SR** at 20K steps (M=128, severe overfitting — model outputs identical action every step). VTR on MLP projector does NOT improve SR; reframed as \"VTR ceiling depends on connector type\" finding. User directive: performance degradation acceptable if efficiency improves — VTR value is 75% KV-cache reduction + attention speedup. VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress to test whether smaller M values fare better.\n\n**Differentiation from concurrent work**: 4 concurrent works (Compressor-VLA, SpecPrune-VLA, LightVLA ICRA'26, See What Matters ICML'26) all propose pruning on MLP-projector VLAs. We (1) explain why pruning fails on pixel-shuffle architectures, (2) identify why pruning succeeds on linear projection (tokens are truly independent), and (3) propose a re-encoding method motivated by the diagnostic analysis.\n\n**Model coverage**: 5 VLA models × 3 connector families × 4 model sizes (450M-7B). RC1 (only 2 models) and RC2 (size confound) fully addressed.\n\n## Core Claims (5 claims, expanded from 4)\n\n### Claim 1: Architecture-Dependent Compressibility (taxonomy — D107 RESOLVED)\nThe effective vision-to-LLM projection pipeline determines pruning robustness. Evidence from 5 VLA models:\n- **Pure linear projection** (π0): immune — k=0.1 loss improves 2.4%\n- **Linear + deep post-processing** (X-VLA, BART 12L): **threshold-graded** — immune k≥0.9 (97.6%), threshold at k=0.7 (56.2%, -43pp), then graded degradation k≤0.5 (42.6%→23.0%→~4%→~0%). Distinct from SmolVLA's catastrophic cliff (any pruning → 0%)\n- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA, OFT): smooth graded degradation. k=0.5 → 37.4% (-49% relative)\n- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA): **catastrophic cliff** — k=0.95 (5% removal) → 0% SR. Any pruning destroys.\n- **CV predicts degradation onset**: 0.038 (immune) → 0.151 (threshold-graded at k=0.7) → 0.215 (immediate onset) → 0.314 (catastrophic cliff)\n\n**Evidence**: 5 models, 3 connector families, 4 model sizes (450M-7B). Key controlled comparison: π0 (256 tokens, linear) k=0.1 = 0.976 vs OpenVLA (256 tokens, 3-layer MLP) k=0.1 = 1.608. Same token count, same encoder lineage, only connector differs. X-VLA cliff pattern (k=0.9: 97.6% → k=0.7: 56.2%) confirms intermediate CV predicts intermediate behavior.\n\n⚠️ **D108: Pruning method discrepancy** — Offline diagnostic uses L2_norm_zero_out (all models). But LIBERO closed-loop evals differ: OpenVLA = random removal (torch.randperm, physical), X-VLA = L2 norm removal (importance-based, physical). SmolVLA = all methods tested (all 0%). This STRENGTHENS findings (OpenVLA survives even random = hardest test; X-VLA cliffs even with importance-based = easiest test), but paper must accurately report. OpenVLA L2 norm comparison experiment planned for fair cross-model comparison.\n\n### Claim 2: Pixel Shuffle Creates Irreversible Token Entanglement\nSmolVLA's pixel_shuffle connector spatially folds 1024 SigLIP patches into 64 tokens per camera (16x compression). Each resulting token encodes a 32x32 pixel region via channel-to-spatial reorganization. This creates extreme cross-token spatial entanglement: removing any single token eliminates an entire spatial quadrant's information with no redundancy to compensate.\n\n**Evidence**:\n- k=0.95 (remove only 7/128 tokens = 5.5%) = 0% SR — even minimal removal is catastrophic\n- k=0.9 (remove 13/128 tokens) = 0% SR\n- Geometric prior (Sobel edge) k=0.5/0.7/0.9 = all 0%\n- Attention entropy ratio 0.952 (near-uniform, TV=0.05)\n- Official checkpoint Object (59.2% baseline) cliff-edge at k=0.5 → 0%\n- Official checkpoint Spatial (43.8% baseline) cliff-edge at k=0.5 → 0.6% (3/500, CI [0.2%, 1.7%])\n\n### Claim 3a: Linear Projection → Depends on Effective Pipeline (D107: RESOLVED)\nPure linear projection (π0): immune. Linear projection + deep post-processing (X-VLA, BART 12L): \"robust-then-cliff\" — immune at k≥0.9, cliff at k=0.7, then graded degradation. The BART encoder introduces non-linear cross-token mixing that explains intermediate CV=0.151 and the cliff pattern.\n\n**Evidence** (X-VLA LIBERO SR — Batch 1 + Batch 2 COMPLETE, full 8-point curve):\n- k=1.0: **99.2%** (baseline, 496/500) — per-task: [98, 100, 98, 100, 100, 96, 100, 100, 100, 100]\n- k=0.95: **99.0%** (-0.2pp) — per-task: [98, 100, 100, 96, 100, 96, 100, 100, 100, 100]\n- k=0.9: **97.6%** (-1.6pp) — per-task: [96, 98, 100, 92, 100, 96, 100, 98, 96, 100]\n- k=0.7: **56.2%** (-43pp, CLIFF — 281/500) — per-task: [94, 2, 100, 80, 28, 92, 12, 66, 0, 88]\n- k=0.5: **42.6%** (-57pp) — Batch 2 confirmed (MSH fix applied)\n- k=0.3: **23.0%** (-77pp) — graded degradation continues below cliff\n- k=0.2: **~4.0%** (-96pp) — near-zero\n- k=0.1: **~0.0%** (-100pp) — complete failure\n✅ Full curve confirms threshold-graded pattern: immune k≥0.9, cliff at k=0.7, then graded degradation k≤0.5 (42.6%→23.0%→~4%→~0%).\n\nπ0 evidence:\n- π0 (3.3B, 256 tokens, pure linear proj): k=0.1 normalized_L1 = 0.976 (-2.4% = improvement), k=0.5 = 0.983\n- Attention entropy: π0 suffix-to-vision mean 0.959 (near-uniform across 18 layers, range [0.931, 0.983])\n- Importance CV: π0 = 0.038 (lowest in spectrum)\n\n**Key insight**: \"Linear projection\" is NOT sufficient for immunity. The effective pipeline matters. X-VLA's BART encoder (12 transformer layers after linear proj) introduces partial dependencies → CV=0.151 → cliff at k=0.7. π0's pure linear proj → CV=0.038 → immune even at k=0.1.\n\n### Claim 3b: MLP Projector → Graded Degradation\nMulti-layer MLP connectors create partial token dependencies through non-linear mixing, enabling graceful but real degradation.\n\n**Evidence** (OpenVLA 6-point degradation curve):\n- k=1.0: 74.0% (baseline)\n- k=0.95: 69.4% (-6% relative)\n- k=0.9: 62.0% (-16% relative)\n- k=0.7: 49.0% (-34% relative)\n- k=0.5: 37.4% (-49% relative)\n- k=0.3: 20.6% (-72% relative)\n- Entropy ratio 0.639 (progressive sharpening L0=0.98→L29=0.48, TV=0.50)\n- OFT (same connector, different action head): entropy 0.667 ≈ Standard 0.661 → connector determines attention structure, not action head\n- CogACT (MLP projector, literature): 74.8% → 74.2% under 78% pruning (EfficientVLA)\n\n### Claim 4: Learned Re-Encoding Overcomes Cliff-Edge Where Deletion Fails (D072+MLP confirmed → upgraded to METHOD per D091)\nTwo independent re-encoding architectures (~22M params each) validate that **any learned re-encoding** can transform entangled pixel_shuffle tokens into effective representations. **The core mechanism is re-encoding itself, not the specific architecture**: cross-attention (60.1±1.3%, 3-seed) and MLP adapter (63.4±2.6%, 3-seed) both recover from 0% hard pruning, with p≈0.15 confirming no significant difference. M=128 passthrough (~60.0%, 2-seed) achieves +15pp over baseline 44.8%, proving the gain comes from re-encoding rather than compression. M=64 achieves best tradeoff at 62.0±2.3% with 50% compression. Cross-suite generalization confirmed: M=32 recovers to 53.2% on Spatial (vs 0.6% pruning cliff-edge) and 56.4% on Goal. M=96 dip statistically confirmed (p=0.034 vs M=64).\n\n**D109 C4-ext on OpenVLA (MLP projector)**: M=128 VTR at 20K steps = **0% SR** (severe overfitting, model outputs identical action every step). This suggests VTR's effectiveness is connector-dependent: pixel-shuffle benefits enormously (0%→60%+) because re-encoding repairs spatial entanglement, while MLP projector tokens are already individually meaningful and VTR adds unnecessary complexity. VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress — if these also fail, VTR is specifically a pixel-shuffle solution, which strengthens the architecture-dependency narrative.\n\n**Evidence** (all confirmed):\n\nCross-attention re-encoding (M sweep, 3-seed where available):\n| M | Compression | SR (3-seed mean±std) | Seeds | Notes |\n|---|------------|-----|-----|-----|\n| 16 | 87.5% | **56.9±1.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ ZERO loss vs M=128 |\n| 32 | 75% | **60.1±1.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ |\n| 64 | 50% | **62.0±2.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ best tradeoff |\n| 96 | 25% | 54.5±3.2% | 42/43/44 | ✅ highest variance |\n| 128 | 0% (passthrough) | **58.0±3.5%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ passthrough control |\n\nMLP adapter control (M=32, ~22.14M params, 3-seed):\n| Architecture | Params | M | Mean SR (3-seed) | Std | Individual seeds |\n|---|---|---|-----|-----|-----|\n| Cross-attention (VTC) | 22.2M | 32 | **60.1%** | ±1.3 | 61.6 / 59.2 / 59.6 |\n| **MLP adapter** | **22.14M** | **32** | **63.4%** | **±2.6** | **65.2 / 64.6 / 60.4** |\n\nTwo-sample t-test: t≈1.94, p≈0.15 → **no significant difference** (α=0.05). Both >> 0% (hard pruning) and > 44.8% (baseline). MLP ≥ VTC in all 3 seeds but difference not statistically significant — confirms re-encoding mechanism, not architecture, is the causal factor. (Note: M=32 seed43 corrected from 62.4% to 59.2% per registry verification; 62.4% was M=96 seed43 CI upper bound misattributed.)\n\n## Story Spine\n\n**Problem**: Vision token efficiency is critical for real-time VLA deployment. Growing literature proposes inference-time token reduction (FastV, VLA-IAP, H2O, ToMe). These methods succeed on some VLAs but their behavior across different architectures is unstudied.\n\n**Gap**: No work has systematically compared token pruning robustness across VLA architectures. The implicit assumption that \"token pruning works or fails uniformly\" is untested. The critical architectural factor determining prunability is unknown.\n\n**Discovery**: We find that the effective vision-to-LLM projection pipeline determines token pruning robustness. Testing 5 VLA models (450M-7B):\n- **Pure linear projection** (π0): immune. k=0.1 loss improves 2.4%.\n- **Linear + deep post-processing** (X-VLA, BART 12L): threshold-graded — robust k≥0.9, threshold at k=0.7 (97.6%→56.2%), then graded below.\n- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA, OFT): smooth graded degradation. k=0.5 → 37.4% (-49%).\n- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA): catastrophic cliff. k=0.95 → 0% SR.\nCV of token importance (0.038→0.151→0.215→0.314) is a continuous predictor: lower CV = later onset of degradation.\n\n**Solution**: Diagnose-then-Compress framework. Step 1: Token importance CV provides zero-cost diagnostic for pruning tolerance (one forward pass). Step 2: VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) provides universal compression. For pixel-shuffle: recovers from 0% to 60%+ SR, M-curve confirmed flat (D105: M=16 56.9% ≈ M=128 58.0%, near-lossless at any compression ratio). For MLP projector: D109 C4-ext = 0% SR (overfitting at M=128); VTC-only M=32/M=64 in progress.\n\n**Headline result**: \"Across 5 VLA models spanning 3 connector architectures, we find that pruning tolerance depends on the effective vision-to-LLM pipeline: pure linear projection is immune (π0: loss improves 2.4% at 90% removal), linear projection with deep post-processing shows a cliff pattern (X-VLA: 97.6% at k=0.9, 56.2% at k=0.7), MLP connectors degrade smoothly (OpenVLA: -49% at 50% removal), and pixel-shuffle collapses catastrophically (SmolVLA: 0% at 5% removal). Token importance CV predicts this spectrum. For vulnerable architectures, VTR achieves 60%+ SR at 75% compression where deletion achieves 0%.\"\n\n## Paper Structure (5-model version)\n\n1. **Introduction**: VLA efficiency motivation → diverse connector architectures → 4-class taxonomy discovery → Diagnose-then-Compress framework\n2. **Background**: 5 VLA models, 3 connector families (linear/MLP/pixel-shuffle), token flow analysis\n3. **Experimental Setup**: 5 models, LIBERO benchmark, pruning protocol, VTR compression, diagnostic metrics\n4. **Main Results**:\n   - §4.1: 4-Class Taxonomy Overview (Table 1: 5 models × pruning sensitivity)\n   - §4.2: Catastrophic — pixel-shuffle cliff-edge (SmolVLA, all configs 0%)\n   - §4.3: Graded — MLP degradation (OpenVLA 6-point curve + OFT entropy confirmation)\n   - §4.4: Immune — linear projection (π0 + X-VLA, controlled comparison with OpenVLA)\n   - §4.5: VTR overcomes cliff-edge (M-curve flat + architecture independence)\n5. **Analysis**:\n   - §5.1: Why pixel_shuffle creates entanglement (spatial folding + controlled comparison)\n   - §5.2: Diagnostic metric — Entropy + CV composite (D104, 4-model validation)\n   - §5.3: Re-encoding mechanism (M=128 passthrough + MLP adapter + M-curve flat D105)\n6. **Discussion**: Design implications, limitations (LIBERO only, no real robot), future work\n7. **Conclusion**: 5 claims summary\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### RC1: Only 2 models → **FULLY ADDRESSED**\n**Response**: Now 5 models (SmolVLA, OpenVLA, OpenVLA-OFT, π0, X-VLA) across 3 connector families (pixel-shuffle, 3-layer MLP, linear projection) and 4 model sizes (450M-7B). Each connector class has ≥2 models.\n\n### RC2: Model size confound (450M vs 7B) → **FULLY ADDRESSED**\n**Response**: π0 (3.3B, linear) is pruning-immune while OpenVLA (7B, MLP) degrades 61% at k=0.1. Larger model is MORE vulnerable, not less — directly falsifies \"larger models are more robust\" hypothesis. X-VLA (880M, linear) also immune, matching π0 behavior despite 4× smaller. Size is not the explanatory variable; connector type is.\n\n### RC3: Why not test SmolVLA without pixel_shuffle?\n**Response**: SmolVLA's connector is integral (LLM expects 128 tokens, not 1024). Removing it requires retraining from scratch. OpenVLA comparison isolates the connector's role.\n\n### RC4: Smart compression — is re-encoding or compression the mechanism?\n**Response**: Two independent lines of evidence. (1) M=128 passthrough control: M=128 (no compression) = 59.8% vs M=32 (75% compression) = 61.6%. The +15pp over baseline comes from re-encoding; compression is a free bonus. (2) Architecture control: MLP adapter (65.2%) ≈ cross-attention (61.6%) with CI overlap — re-encoding works regardless of the specific mechanism. Both lines converge: the causal factor is learned re-encoding, not cross-attention specifically nor compression.\n\n### RC5: Relationship to VLA-IAP\n**Response**: VLA-IAP's 97.8% on OpenVLA is consistent with our finding: MLP projector preserves token independence. VLA-IAP untested on pixel_shuffle VLAs; our geometric prior experiments (0%) predict it would fail.\n\n### RC6: Is this just \"different models behave differently\"?\n**Response**: We identify the specific mechanism (pixel_shuffle spatial folding) and provide evidence for WHY. Concrete design implications: future VLAs wanting efficiency should avoid pixel_shuffle or include learned re-encoding modules.\n\n## All Experimental Evidence (confirmed)\n\n### SmolVLA Cliff-Edge\n- Fine-tuned baseline (Object): 44.8% (224/500)\n- 6 pruning conditions (random/ACIS/ToMe × k=0.5/0.7/0.9): all 0%\n- Geometric prior (Sobel) k=0.5/0.7/0.9: all 0%\n- Attention entropy: 0.952 (flat, TV=0.05)\n- Official checkpoint Object: 59.2% → 0% at k=0.5\n- Official checkpoint Spatial: 43.8% → 0.6% (3/500, CI [0.2%, 1.7%]) at k=0.5 — near-zero, confirms cliff-edge across suites\n\n### OpenVLA Degradation Curve\n- k=1.0: 74.0% (370/500)\n- k=0.95: 69.4% (-6% relative)\n- k=0.9: 62.0% (-16% relative)\n- k=0.7: 49.0% (245/500, -34% relative)\n- k=0.5: 37.4% (187/500, -49% relative)\n- k=0.3: 20.6% (103/500, -72% relative)\n- Entropy: 0.639 (progressive sharpening, TV=0.50)\n\n### Cross-Model Pruning Taxonomy (NEW — D100 confirmed all L2_norm_zero_out)\n| Model | Connector | Tokens | k=0.1 norm_L1 | k=0.5 norm_L1 | Class |\n|-------|-----------|--------|---------------|---------------|-------|\n| π0 (3.3B) | Pure linear proj | 256 | 0.976 (-2.4%) | 0.983 | Immune |\n| X-VLA (880M) | Linear + BART 12L | 50 | ~1.00 | ~1.00 | Threshold-graded (k=0.7: 56.2%) |\n| OpenVLA (7B) | 3-layer MLP | 256 | 1.608 (+61%) | 1.167 (+17%) | Smooth graded |\n| OFT (7B) | 3-layer MLP | 256 | pending (M031) | — | (entropy=0.667≈Std) |\n| SmolVLA (450M) | Pixel-shuffle | 128 | — | 0% cliff | Catastrophic |\n\nDiagnostic metrics (D104+D106: CV as continuous predictor):\n| Model | Connector (effective) | Entropy | CV | Pruning Behavior |\n|-------|----------------------|---------|------|------------------|\n| π0 | Pure linear proj | 0.959 | 0.038 | Immune (offline, k=0.1 improves) |\n| X-VLA | Linear proj + BART enc (12L) | **0.614** | **0.151** | Threshold-graded: robust k≥0.9, cliff k=0.7 (56.2%) |\n| OpenVLA | 3-layer MLP (GELU) | 0.661 | 0.215 | Graded (74→37.4% at k=0.5) |\n| OFT | 3-layer MLP (GELU) | 0.667 | — | (entropy≈Standard, confirms connector) |\n| SmolVLA | Pixel-shuffle (16×) | 0.952 | **0.314** | Catastrophic (0% at k=0.95) |\n\nKey insights (updated with X-VLA data):\n1. **CV is a continuous predictor**: 0.038 → 0.151 → 0.215 → 0.314 maps to decreasing pruning tolerance. NOT a 3-class discrete classifier.\n2. **X-VLA CV=0.151 correctly predicted its intermediate behavior** — closer to OpenVLA (0.215) than π0 (0.038), matching k=0.7 SR ≈ OpenVLA k=0.7.\n3. **X-VLA entropy=0.614 ≈ OpenVLA 0.661** — both have BART/MLP non-linear mixing. X-VLA is NOT \"high entropy\" like π0.\n4. **Effective connector complexity matters more than nominal label**: X-VLA is \"linear proj\" but BART encoder introduces 12 transformer layers of mixing. Paper should discuss \"effective connector\" = projection + any intermediate processing.\n5. OFT entropy 0.667 ≈ Standard 0.661 → action head does not affect attention structure\n6. Framing: CV captures \"degree of non-linear mixing in the vision-to-LLM pathway.\" More mixing → higher CV → less tolerant of pruning.\n\n### Smart Compress (Learned Re-encoding)\nCross-attention (VTC) M sweep (3-seed where available):\n- M=16: **56.9% ± 1.3pp** (3-seed: 55.8/58.4/56.5) — 87.5% compression, ZERO loss vs M=128\n- M=32: 60.1±1.3% (3-seed: 61.6/59.2/59.6)\n- M=64: 62.0±2.3% (3-seed: 61.6/60.0/64.4)\n- M=96: 54.5±3.2% (3-seed: 52.6/58.2/52.8) — highest variance\n- M=128: 58.0±3.5pp (3-seed: 59.8/54.0/60.2) — passthrough control\n- **D102 CONFIRMED: M-curve is flat.** M=16 (56.9%) = M=128 (58.0%), difference < 1.1pp. VTC achieves near-lossless compression at ANY ratio for pixel-shuffle connector. All M values within ±5pp of baseline ~59%.\n\nMLP adapter (M=32, 3-seed):\n- seed42: 65.2% (326/500), seed43: 64.6% (323/500), seed44: 60.4% (302/500)\n- Mean: 63.4% ± 2.6 vs VTC M=32 mean 60.1% ± 1.3\n- t-test p≈0.15, no significant difference — confirms architecture-independence\n\n### D109: VTR on OpenVLA (MLP projector) — FAILED\n- C4-ext M=128 at 20K steps: **0% SR** (0/44 episodes before eval termination)\n- Failure mode: model outputs identical action every timestep (severe overfitting)\n- Interpretation: VTR adds unnecessary complexity for MLP projector tokens (already individually meaningful). VTR specifically solves pixel-shuffle entanglement.\n- VTC-only M=32 and M=64 training in progress on westd-41074:2-3\n\n### Cross-Suite VTR Generalization (SmolVLA)\n- M=32 Spatial: 53.2% (vs official Spatial baseline 43.8%, vs pruning 0.6% — recovery from cliff-edge AND exceeds uncompressed baseline)\n- M=32 Goal: 56.4% (vs official Goal baseline 63.0%, vs pruning 0% — recovery from cliff-edge but below uncompressed baseline; frame as compression-recovery, not performance boost)\n- Note: VTR trained on Object suite, evaluated cross-suite. Official baselines from different checkpoint (official vs LoRA-FT); comparisons should emphasize recovery from 0% rather than absolute performance vs uncompressed.\n\n### Pairwise Statistical Tests (Welch's t-test, n=3 per condition)\n- M=32 VTC vs M=32 MLP: p=0.150 (not significant) — confirms architecture-independence\n- M=64 VTC vs M=96 VTC: p=0.034 (significant) — M=96 dip confirmed real\n- M=32 MLP vs M=96 VTC: p=0.022 (significant) — M=96 underperforms\n- M=32/M=64/M=128 VTC cluster: all pairwise p>0.25 — robust across M values\n- Bonferroni note: no pair survives correction at 10 tests; n=3 limits power (~0.2 for medium effects)\n\n### Supplementary\n- Inference latency: 6% speedup at M=32\n- KV-cache: 75% memory reduction at M=32\n","numLines":267,"startLine":1,"totalLines":267}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015m6hGLBL8HHSsjx3dnqCTQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"SmolVLA VTR 3-seed aggregation completion (M=16, M=128)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"M=16 seed43/44和M=128 seed43的training已完成（ANALYZING），eval数据已全部采集。 确认3-seed聚合数值。此plan实质已完成，status应更新为complete。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"m16_3seed_mean_sr\": 56.9,\n7\t      \"m16_3seed_std\": 1.3,\n8\t      \"m16_seeds\": {\n9\t        \"seed42\": 55.8,\n10\t        \"seed43\": 58.4,\n11\t        \"seed44\": 56.5\n12\t      },\n13\t      \"m128_3seed_mean_sr\": 58.0,\n14\t      \"m128_3seed_std\": 3.5,\n15\t      \"m128_seeds\": {\n16\t        \"seed42\": 59.8,\n17\t        \"seed43\": 54.0,\n18\t        \"seed44\": 60.2\n19\t      },\n20\t      \"m_curve_flat_confirmed\": true,\n21\t      \"max_m_diff_pp\": 1.1\n22\t    },\n23\t    \"tables\": [\n24\t      {\n25\t        \"name\": \"SmolVLA VTR完整M-sweep (3-seed confirmed)\",\n26\t        \"data\": \"| M   | 压缩率  | Seed42 | Seed43 | Seed44 | Mean±Std      |\\n|-----|---------|--------|--------|--------|---------------|\\n| 16  | 87.5%   | 55.8%  | 58.4%  | 56.5%  | 56.9 ± 1.3%  |\\n| 32  | 75%     | 61.6%  | 59.2%  | 59.6%  | 60.1 ± 1.3%  |\\n| 64  | 50%     | 61.6%  | 60.0%  | 64.4%  | 62.0 ± 2.3%  |\\n| 96  | 25%     | 52.6%  | 58.2%  | 52.8%  | 54.5 ± 3.2%  |\\n| 128 | 0%      | 59.8%  | 54.0%  | 60.2%  | 58.0 ± 3.5%  |\\n\"\n27\t      }\n28\t    ],\n29\t    \"figures\": [],\n30\t    \"analysis\": \"已完成。M-curve flat是VTR on pixel-shuffle的核心发现： re-encoding而非compression是因果因子。任何压缩比下均near-lossless。\\n\\n\\n数据已全部在registry中确认。M=16 (56.9±1.3%) ≈ M=128 (58.0±3.5%)， 差异<1.1pp。M-curve flatness是confirmed fact (D105)。 M=128 seed43的54.0%是该seed下特定task表现偏弱导致（cream_cheese 32.2%, ketchup 34.8%均显著低于其他seed），但不影响核心结论。 所有5个M值的3-seed mean均在baseline ~59%的±5pp内。 此plan_id实质已完成，无需预测。\\n\"\n31\t  },\n32\t  {\n33\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTR M=128 全量 (已confirmed negative)\",\n34\t    \"description\": \"VTR (cross-attention compressor + decoder) M=128在OpenVLA上20K步评估。 已确认0% SR——严重过拟合，模型每步输出identical action。\\n\",\n35\t    \"results\": {\n36\t      \"openvla_vtr_m128_sr\": 0,\n37\t      \"episodes_evaluated\": 44,\n38\t      \"failure_mode\": \"identical action every timestep\",\n39\t      \"overfitting_severity\": \"complete — model collapsed to single-action policy\"\n40\t    },\n41\t    \"tables\": [],\n42\t    \"figures\": [],\n43\t    \"analysis\": \"已完成。0% SR将作为Claim 4 negative evidence呈现： \\\"VTR ceiling depends on connector type — pixel-shuffle benefits enormously (0%→60%+) while MLP projector suffers (74%→0%).\\\"\\n\\n\\nMLP projector的3层GELU已将SigLIP patch embeddings投射为LLM-ready tokens， 每个token独立承载语义（CV=0.215，moderate heterogeneity但无空间纠缠）。 VTR的cross-attention将256个独立token强制经过bottleneck再decode， 这对已经独立的tokens是destructive operation：(1) 引入了不必要的信息混合， (2) 22M额外参数在LIBERO的小规模数据（~50 demo/task）上快速过拟合， (3) 20K步已足够让compressor学会\\\"记住\\\"训练分布而非泛化。 对比SmolVLA：pixel-shuffle tokens确实需要re-encoding来解空间纠缠， 所以同样的VTR在那里成功（0%→60%+）。 此failure本身是median档叙事的核心evidence。\\n\"\n44\t  },\n45\t  {\n46\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC-only M=32 (75%压缩)\",\n47\t    \"description\": \"仅cross-attention compressor（无decoder），M=32，在OpenVLA上训练。 测试VTC-only是否能避免full VTR M=128的过拟合。 当前状态：train_openvla_sc_m32_vtconly_seed42 RUNNING。\\n\",\n48\t    \"results\": {\n49\t      \"openvla_vtconly_m32_sr\": 7,\n50\t      \"openvla_vtconly_m32_sr_range\": [\n51\t        0,\n52\t        15\n53\t      ],\n54\t      \"openvla_vtconly_m32_failure_mode\": \"severe degradation, possible partial overfitting\"\n55\t    },\n56\t    \"tables\": [\n57\t      {\n58\t        \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC-only M-sweep predicted results\",\n59\t        \"data\": \"| M   | 压缩率  | 预测SR     | 预测区间     | vs Baseline 74% |\\n|-----|---------|-----------|------------|----------------|\\n| 32  | 75%     | ~7%       | [0%, 15%]  | -91% relative  |\\n| 64  | 50%     | ~4%       | [0%, 15%]  | -95% relative  |\\n| 96  | 62.5%保留| ~2%       | [0%, 10%]  | -97% relative  |\\n| 128 | 0% (VTR)| 0%        | confirmed  | -100%          |\\n\"\n60\t      }\n61\t    ],\n62\t    \"figures\": [],\n63\t    \"analysis\": \"M=32的strong compression理论上是最有可能\\\"accidentally work\\\"的配置： (1) 参数最少→过拟合风险最低，(2) 信息压缩最极端→如果某些token确实冗余 则可能保留核心信息。但MLP projector的CV=0.215意味着tokens间heterogeneity 不够极端（不像SmolVLA CV=0.314的空间纠缠），没有\\\"需要被解开的结构\\\" 供cross-attention利用。预测SR<15%。\\n\\n\\n核心问题未变：MLP projector tokens不需要re-encoding。VTC-only去掉了decoder （减少约11M参数），但cross-attention compressor仍将256个token压缩到32个query。 这对MLP projector是根本性错误——每个original token独立承载语义， cross-attention将8个token的信息挤进1个query（256/32=8:1）， 不同于pixel-shuffle tokens中spatial信息可通过re-encoding恢复。 M=32的强压缩可能提供些许regularization（相比M=128）， 所以过拟合可能没那么complete，但SR仍将极低。 少数\\\"简单\\\"task可能偶尔成功（如chocolate_pudding在OpenVLA baseline中>80%）， 但overall SR远低于baseline 74%。预测0-15%，中位数~7%。\\n\"\n64\t  },\n65\t  {\n66\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC-only M=64 (50%压缩)\",\n67\t    \"description\": \"VTC-only M=64在OpenVLA上训练。 当前状态：train_openvla_sc_m64_seed42_v3 RUNNING。\\n\",\n68\t    \"results\": {\n69\t      \"openvla_vtconly_m64_sr\": 4,\n70\t      \"openvla_vtconly_m64_sr_range\": [\n71\t        0,\n72\t        15\n73\t      ]\n74\t    },\n75\t    \"tables\": [],\n76\t    \"figures\": [],\n77\t    \"analysis\": \"M=64结果与M=32共同形成OpenVLA VTC-only M-sweep。 无论具体数值排序如何（M=32 > M=64 or M=32 < M=64）， 只要全部<15%就确认VTR/VTC对MLP projector无效。\\n\\n\\nM=64保留50%的token数。M=128 full VTR已0%，M=64 VTC-only减少了decoder 但仍有cross-attention bottleneck。比M=32的regularization弱（更多参数自由度）， 比M=128少了decoder。如果过拟合是dominant failure mode（M=128 evidence支持此判断）， M=64介于M=32和M=128之间，可能比M=32稍差。 但如果压缩损失是dominant failure mode，M=64应比M=32好（保留更多信息）。 在median档下，过拟合是主因→M=64可能≤M=32。预测~4%，区间[0, 15%]。\\n\"\n78\t  },\n79\t  {\n80\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC-only M=96 (25%压缩)\",\n81\t    \"description\": \"VTC-only M=96在OpenVLA上训练。最接近passthrough（96/256=37.5%保留）。 当前状态：train_openvla_sc_m96_seed42_v3 RUNNING。\\n\",\n82\t    \"results\": {\n83\t      \"openvla_vtconly_m96_sr\": 2,\n84\t      \"openvla_vtconly_m96_sr_range\": [\n85\t        0,\n86\t        10\n87\t      ]\n88\t    },\n89\t    \"tables\": [],\n90\t    \"figures\": [],\n91\t    \"analysis\": \"三个M值形成的M-sweep pattern本身是informative的： 如果SmolVLA M-curve flat而OpenVLA M-curve monotonically decreasing（或all near 0%）， 这两条曲线的对比就是一张figure。\\n\\n\\nM=96 VTC-only最接近M=128的configuration——压缩比最低，参数自由度最大。 M=128 full VTR的0%主要由过拟合导致，M=96 VTC-only虽去掉decoder但 compressor参数仍然很多（96个query × hidden_dim）。 在三个M值中最容易过拟合，预测为最差。~2%，区间[0, 10%]。 若M=96≈0%且M=32~7%，则形成inverse M-curve（越大的M越差）， 与SmolVLA的flat M-curve形成sharp contrast——进一步支持 \\\"VTR的行为本身取决于connector type\\\"的论点。\\n\"\n92\t  },\n93\t  {\n94\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.95 (5% removal)\",\n95\t    \"description\": \"L2 norm importance-based pruning k=0.95在OpenVLA上。 统一pruning method与X-VLA（两者均L2 norm）。 对比：random pruning k=0.95 = 69.4%。 当前状态：eval_openvla_prune_l2norm_k095 RUNNING。\\n\",\n96\t    \"results\": {\n97\t      \"openvla_l2norm_k095_sr\": 70,\n98\t      \"openvla_l2norm_k095_sr_range\": [\n99\t        59,\n100\t        79\n101\t      ],\n102\t      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": \"+0.6\"\n103\t    },\n104\t    \"tables\": [],\n105\t    \"figures\": [],\n106\t    \"analysis\": \"k=0.95是两种方法差异最小的数据点。 用于完善L2 norm全曲线，与random曲线overlay展示method invariance。\\n\\n\\nk=0.95仅移除13/256 = 5%的token。在如此低的removal ratio下， importance-based (L2 norm) vs random的差异被两个因素压缩到极小： (1) 被移除的13个token中，L2 norm选中的\\\"最不重要\\\"vs随机选中的差异有限—— MLP projector CV=0.215意味着importance分布的tail不极端； (2) 500 episodes的statistical power在1-2pp的difference下不足以detect。 Random=69.4%。L2 norm预测~70%（可能69-72%），差异在统计噪声内。 核心论点不受影响：无论pruning method，MLP projector在k=0.95保持>90%性能。\\n\"\n107\t  },\n108\t  {\n109\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.9 (10% removal)\",\n110\t    \"description\": \"L2 norm k=0.9在OpenVLA上。对比random k=0.9 = 62.0%。 当前状态：eval_openvla_prune_l2norm_k09 RUNNING。\\n\",\n111\t    \"results\": {\n112\t      \"openvla_l2norm_k09_sr\": 63,\n113\t      \"openvla_l2norm_k09_sr_range\": [\n114\t        52,\n115\t        72\n116\t      ],\n117\t      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": \"+1\"\n118\t    },\n119\t    \"tables\": [\n120\t      {\n121\t        \"name\": \"Cross-model L2 norm k=0.9对比\",\n122\t        \"data\": \"| Model   | Connector       | CV    | L2 norm k=0.9 SR | 对比baseline |\\n|---------|-----------------|-------|------------------|-------------|\\n| π0      | Pure linear     | 0.038 | ~99% (offline)   | -0.7%       |\\n| X-VLA   | Linear+BART 12L | 0.151 | 97.6%            | -1.6pp      |\\n| OpenVLA | 3-layer MLP     | 0.215 | ~63%             | -15% rel    |\\n| SmolVLA | Pixel-shuffle   | 0.314 | 0%               | -100%       |\\n\"\n123\t      }\n124\t    ],\n125\t    \"figures\": [],\n126\t    \"analysis\": \"k=0.9是论文中cross-model comparison的关键k值： 所有4个model在同一pruning method下的对比清晰展示taxonomy。 L2 norm unified protocol使得cross-model comparison methodologically clean。\\n\\n\\nk=0.9移除26/256 = 10%的token。L2 norm有一点点空间选择性保留重要token， 但26个token中importance ranking的真正差异仍然有限。 Random=62%。L2 norm可能有marginal improvement to ~63%（1pp）， 但也可能恰好worse by 1-2pp due to sampling variance。 重要的是：62%±5pp，仍在\\\"graded degradation\\\"的范畴内， 与X-VLA k=0.9 (97.6%, robust) 形成stark contrast—— OpenVLA在10% removal就已经-16% relative，X-VLA还几乎无损。 这直接isolate connector effect：same pruning method, same k, different degradation pattern。\\n\"\n127\t  },\n128\t  {\n129\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.7 (30% removal)\",\n130\t    \"description\": \"L2 norm k=0.7。对比random k=0.7 = 49.0%。 此k值是X-VLA cliff point (56.2%)的对照。\\n\",\n131\t    \"results\": {\n132\t      \"openvla_l2norm_k07_sr\": 51,\n133\t      \"openvla_l2norm_k07_sr_range\": [\n134\t        42,\n135\t        58\n136\t      ],\n137\t      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": \"+2\"\n138\t    },\n139\t    \"tables\": [],\n140\t    \"figures\": [],\n141\t    \"analysis\": \"OpenVLA k=0.7 L2 norm是统一protocol下最重要的cross-model对比点之一。 与X-VLA同k同method但degradation pattern截然不同，直接isolate connector effect。\\n\\n\\nk=0.7移除30%的token。L2 norm的importance-based selection在较大removal ratio下 有更多空间发挥——30%中最不重要的token确实可以被识别。 但OpenVLA CV=0.215意味着importance分布不极端（不像SmolVLA CV=0.314）， L2 norm vs random的差距仍然modest。 Random=49%，L2 norm预测~51%（+2pp），区间[42, 58]。 关键cross-model对比：OpenVLA L2 norm k=0.7 ~51% vs X-VLA L2 norm k=0.7 = 56.2%。 两者数值接近但模式不同——OpenVLA是smooth curve上的一点（k=0.9: 63% → k=0.7: 51%, delta=-12pp），X-VLA是cliff-edge（k=0.9: 97.6% → k=0.7: 56.2%, delta=-41pp）。\\n\"\n142\t  },\n143\t  {\n144\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.5 (50% removal)\",\n145\t    \"description\": \"L2 norm k=0.5。对比random k=0.5 = 37.4%。\\n\",\n146\t    \"results\": {\n147\t      \"openvla_l2norm_k05_sr\": 40,\n148\t      \"openvla_l2norm_k05_sr_range\": [\n149\t        30,\n150\t        47\n151\t      ],\n152\t      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": \"+3\"\n153\t    },\n154\t    \"tables\": [],\n155\t    \"figures\": [],\n156\t    \"analysis\": \"50% removal下L2 norm的优势最可能visible——保留最重要的一半token。 MLP projector的CV=0.215意味着top-50% vs random-50%在信息量上有 measurable但不dramatic的差异。Random=37.4%，L2 norm预测~40%（+3pp）。 +3pp是500 episodes下可detect的差异（Wilson CI width ~±4pp）， 但单次实验不一定statistically significant。 即使L2 norm优势达到+5pp (42%)，仍然是severe degradation vs baseline 74%， taxonomy classification不变（smooth graded）。\\n\"\n157\t  },\n158\t  {\n159\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.3 (70% removal)\",\n160\t    \"description\": \"L2 norm k=0.3。对比random k=0.3 = 20.6%。\\n\",\n161\t    \"results\": {\n162\t      \"openvla_l2norm_k03_sr\": 23,\n163\t      \"openvla_l2norm_k03_sr_range\": [\n164\t        15,\n165\t        30\n166\t      ],\n167\t      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": \"+2\"\n168\t    },\n169\t    \"tables\": [\n170\t      {\n171\t        \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2 norm vs Random完整对比（含预测）\",\n172\t        \"data\": \"| k    | Random SR | L2-norm SR | Delta  | 解读                        |\\n|------|-----------|------------|--------|-----------------------------|\\n| 1.0  | 74.0%     | 74.0%      | 0      | baseline, 无pruning          |\\n| 0.95 | 69.4%     | ~70%       | ~+0.6  | 差异在noise内                |\\n| 0.9  | 62.0%     | ~63%       | ~+1    | marginal L2 advantage        |\\n| 0.7  | 49.0%     | ~51%       | ~+2    | visible但modest advantage    |\\n| 0.5  | 37.4%     | ~40%       | ~+3    | L2 advantage最大点           |\\n| 0.3  | 20.6%     | ~23%       | ~+2    | extreme removal, 优势缩小    |\\n\"\n173\t      }\n174\t    ],\n175\t    \"figures\": [],\n176\t    \"analysis\": \"L2 norm全曲线确认：OpenVLA graded degradation与pruning方法无关。 两条曲线的near-overlap是taxonomy robustness的直接evidence。 论文可一句话总结：\\\"L2-norm和random pruning在OpenVLA上产生near-identical degradation curves (Δ<3pp across all k), confirming that connector type — not pruning strategy — determines pruning tolerance.\\\"\\n\\n\\n70% removal是extreme。L2 norm在此能保留最关键的30%， 但绝对信息损失已很大。Random=20.6%，L2 norm预测~23%。 在此极端条件下，L2 norm的marginal advantage开始diminish—— 即使保留了最重要的30%，remaining 30%中也有很多重要token被丢弃。 两种方法都在20-25%区间内挣扎。\\n\"\n177\t  },\n178\t  {\n179\t    \"name\": \"X-VLA L2-norm pruning k=0.7 seed44 (cliff variance)\",\n180\t    \"description\": \"X-VLA k=0.7使用seed44重复。验证cliff位置的seed robustness。 Seed42 = 56.2%。当前状态：eval_xvla_prune_k07_seed44 RUNNING。\\n\",\n181\t    \"results\": {\n182\t      \"xvla_k07_seed44_sr\": 52,\n183\t      \"xvla_k07_seed44_sr_range\": [\n184\t        40,\n185\t        70\n186\t      ],\n187\t      \"cliff_pattern_preserved\": true\n188\t    },\n189\t    \"tables\": [\n190\t      {\n191\t        \"name\": \"X-VLA cliff-point seed variance\",\n192\t        \"data\": \"| k    | Seed42  | Seed44 (pred) | 2-seed Mean | Interpretation          |\\n|------|---------|---------------|-------------|-------------------------|\\n| 1.0  | 99.2%   | ~99%          | ~99%        | baseline stable         |\\n| 0.95 | 99.0%   | ~98%          | ~98.5%      | robust region           |\\n| 0.9  | 97.6%   | ~96.5%        | ~97%        | robust region           |\\n| 0.7  | 56.2%   | ~52%          | ~54%        | CLIFF — high variance   |\\n| 0.5  | 42.6%   | ~40%          | ~41%        | below cliff, stabilizes |\\n\"\n193\t      }\n194\t    ],\n195\t    \"figures\": [],\n196\t    \"analysis\": \"Cliff variance是expected phenomenon（不是noise），可以直接在论文中讨论： \\\"cliff位置在k~0.7处，但exact SR在不同seed下波动±10pp， reflecting the stochastic nature of dependency breaking when token removal crosses the critical threshold.\\\" 若seed44 < 45%，cliff比seed42更sharp → 更强的evidence； 若seed44 > 60%，cliff更shallow → 仍然是>30pp drop from k=0.9。\\n\\n\\nk=0.7是X-VLA的cliff point——从k=0.9的97.6%骤降到56.2% (seed42)。 Cliff points天然high-variance，原因是： (1) BART encoder的12层transformer mixing创建了partial token dependencies， 在k=0.7恰好跨过dependencies被破坏的threshold； (2) seed决定eval episodes的随机初始状态和token removal order， cliff附近某些task的成功高度依赖于具体哪些token被保留； (3) Seed42的per-task分析：task1=2%, task4=28%, task6=12%, task8=0% vs task0=94%, task2=100%——bimodality极端。 seed44的specific task分布会不同，可能某些在seed42失败的task反而成功， 反之亦然。预测overall 40-70%，中位数~52%。 无论具体数值，只要k=0.9 >> k=0.7（>30pp gap），cliff pattern就成立。\\n\"\n197\t  },\n198\t  {\n199\t    \"name\": \"X-VLA L2-norm pruning k=0.9 seed44 (robust region)\",\n200\t    \"description\": \"X-VLA k=0.9 seed44。Seed42 = 97.6%。验证robust region稳定性。 当前状态：eval_xvla_prune_k09_seed44 RUNNING。\\n\",\n201\t    \"results\": {\n202\t      \"xvla_k09_seed44_sr\": 96.5,\n203\t      \"xvla_k09_seed44_sr_range\": [\n204\t        94,\n205\t        99\n206\t      ]\n207\t    },\n208\t    \"tables\": [],\n209\t    \"figures\": [],\n210\t    \"analysis\": \"k=0.9 seed44的高SR（>94%）与k=0.7 seed44的cliff（~52%） 共同确认threshold-graded pattern的定性stability。 2-seed evidence足以支持论文claim（加上per-task breakdown更convincing）。\\n\\n\\nk=0.9在robust region内（cliff在k=0.7）。仅移除10% token。 BART encoder的partial dependencies在此ratio下未被破坏—— 50个token中移除5个，保留的45个token仍足以覆盖绝大多数spatial和semantic信息。 Seed variance在robust region天然很小：不同seed改变的是\\\"哪5个token被移除\\\"， 但L2 norm保证移除的是importance最低的5个，这些token在所有seed下都是 relatively dispensable的。Seed42=97.6%，seed44预测~96.5%（可能95-99%）。\\n\"\n211\t  },\n212\t  {\n213\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.7 seed43\",\n214\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.7 seed43重复。Seed42 = 49.0%。 当前状态：eval_openvla_prune_random_k07_seed43_v2 RUNNING。\\n\",\n215\t    \"results\": {\n216\t      \"openvla_random_k07_seed43_sr\": 47,\n217\t      \"openvla_random_k07_seed43_sr_range\": [\n218\t        40,\n219\t        56\n220\t      ]\n221\t    },\n222\t    \"tables\": [],\n223\t    \"figures\": [],\n224\t    \"analysis\": \"Seed43的一致性确认OpenVLA smooth degradation的reproducibility。 与X-VLA k=0.7的high seed variance形成对比—— \\\"smooth degradation is reproducible, cliff is stochastic.\\\"\\n\\n\\nOpenVLA k=0.7在smooth degradation curve上（不是cliff point）， seed variance应显著低于X-VLA k=0.7。MLP projector的partial independence 意味着不同random mask导致的信息损失是relatively consistent的—— 没有特定token的移除会cause catastrophic failure（不像X-VLA的critical tokens）。 500 episodes × 10 tasks提供了good statistical power。 Seed42=49%，seed43预测47%（±5pp）。 如果delta<3pp，则single-seed结果高度representative。\\n\"\n225\t  },\n226\t  {\n227\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.5 seed43\",\n228\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.5 seed43。Seed42 = 37.4%。 当前状态：eval_openvla_prune_random_k05_seed43_v2 RUNNING。\\n\",\n229\t    \"results\": {\n230\t      \"openvla_random_k05_seed43_sr\": 36,\n231\t      \"openvla_random_k05_seed43_sr_range\": [\n232\t        30,\n233\t        44\n234\t      ]\n235\t    },\n236\t    \"tables\": [],\n237\t    \"figures\": [],\n238\t    \"analysis\": \"同k=0.7的推理。k=0.5移除50%，random mask的具体配置差异更大， 所以seed variance可能比k=0.7稍高（±4pp vs ±3pp）。 但MLP projector的graded特性保证不会出现cliff-like discontinuity。 Seed42=37.4%，seed43预测~36%。若在33-41%范围内均合理。\\n\"\n239\t  },\n240\t  {\n241\t    \"name\": \"RoboFlamingo Perceiver Resampler baseline + pruning sweep\",\n242\t    \"description\": \"在LIBERO上fine-tune RoboFlamingo (Perceiver Resampler connector)， 然后执行pruning sweep。验证第4种connector family的pruning行为。 状态：planned，未开始。\\n\",\n243\t    \"results\": {\n244\t      \"will_complete_before_deadline\": false,\n245\t      \"baseline_sr_if_run\": 45,\n246\t      \"baseline_sr_range\": [\n247\t        35,\n248\t        55\n249\t      ],\n250\t      \"perceiver_cv_prediction\": 0.15,\n251\t      \"perceiver_cv_range\": [\n252\t        0.1,\n253\t        0.2\n254\t      ],\n255\t      \"pruning_k09_sr_if_run\": 40,\n256\t      \"pruning_k07_sr_if_run\": 25,\n257\t      \"pruning_behavior\": \"moderate graded, possibly with soft threshold\"\n258\t    },\n259\t    \"tables\": [\n260\t      {\n261\t        \"name\": \"完整taxonomy预测（含Perceiver Resampler）\",\n262\t        \"data\": \"| Connector         | Model         | CV    | k=0.9 SR | k=0.7 SR | Pattern         | Status    |\\n|-------------------|---------------|-------|----------|----------|-----------------|-----------|\\n| Pure linear       | π0 3.3B       | 0.038 | ~99%     | ~99%     | Immune          | Confirmed |\\n| Linear+BART 12L   | X-VLA 880M    | 0.151 | 97.6%    | 56.2%    | Threshold-graded| Confirmed |\\n| Perceiver Resamp. | RoboFlamingo  | ~0.15 | ~40%?    | ~25%?    | Soft graded?    | Predicted |\\n| 3-layer MLP       | OpenVLA 7B    | 0.215 | 62%      | 49%      | Smooth graded   | Confirmed |\\n| Pixel-shuffle 16× | SmolVLA 450M  | 0.314 | 0%       | 0%       | Catastrophic    | Confirmed |\\n\"\n263\t      }\n264\t    ],\n265\t    \"figures\": [],\n266\t    \"analysis\": \"在median档下，RoboFlamingo不会完成。论文以5模型×3 connector families提交。 Perceiver Resampler作为Discussion section的future work： \\\"Our taxonomy and CV diagnostic predict Perceiver Resampler (used in Flamingo) would show intermediate behavior (CV~0.15); validation is left to future work.\\\" 这是acceptable的——4 confirmed connector types + 5 models已是 most comprehensive cross-architecture VLA token analysis。 Reviewer可能要求但可以argue coverage已足够。 如果reviewer要求且有revision opportunity，可作为revision deliverable。\\n\\nPerceiver Resampler使用learnable query tokens通过cross-attention从encoder output中提取固定数量的compressed representations。架构上与VTC类似 （都是cross-attention压缩），但位于connector（而非compression module）。 预测CV=0.10-0.20（between π0=0.038 and OpenVLA=0.215）： (1) cross-attention引入了soft inter-token dependencies（类似BART）， (2) 但每个query token attend to all encoder tokens（global receptive field）， 信息分布比MLP projector更structured但比pixel-shuffle less entangled。 pruning行为预测：moderate graded degradation，可能在k~0.8有soft threshold （类似X-VLA但更gentle）——Perceiver的global attention给每个token 提供了more redundancy than MLP but less than pure linear。\\n但此实验需要至少3-5天：(1) RoboFlamingo codebase adaptation (~1天), (2) LIBERO data loading + fine-tuning pipeline (~0.5天 setup + 1天 training), (3) pruning sweep + evaluation (~1天), (4) analysis (~0.5天)。 距离abstract deadline (May 26) 仅6天，距离paper deadline (May 29) 仅9天。 无法在deadline前完成。\\n\"\n267\t  }\n268\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb0141ba-9b41-4c32-a6f9-94e34c15fbb4","uuid":"6d2e73a2-55de-4d32-9d99-a5cd7df20288","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:28:05.494Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T155932/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SmolVLA VTR 3-seed aggregation completion (M=16, M=128)\",\n    \"description\": \"M=16 seed43/44和M=128 seed43的training已完成（ANALYZING），eval数据已全部采集。 确认3-seed聚合数值。此plan实质已完成，status应更新为complete。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"m16_3seed_mean_sr\": 56.9,\n      \"m16_3seed_std\": 1.3,\n      \"m16_seeds\": {\n        \"seed42\": 55.8,\n        \"seed43\": 58.4,\n        \"seed44\": 56.5\n      },\n      \"m128_3seed_mean_sr\": 58.0,\n      \"m128_3seed_std\": 3.5,\n      \"m128_seeds\": {\n        \"seed42\": 59.8,\n        \"seed43\": 54.0,\n        \"seed44\": 60.2\n      },\n      \"m_curve_flat_confirmed\": true,\n      \"max_m_diff_pp\": 1.1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"SmolVLA VTR完整M-sweep (3-seed confirmed)\",\n        \"data\": \"| M   | 压缩率  | Seed42 | Seed43 | Seed44 | Mean±Std      |\\n|-----|---------|--------|--------|--------|---------------|\\n| 16  | 87.5%   | 55.8%  | 58.4%  | 56.5%  | 56.9 ± 1.3%  |\\n| 32  | 75%     | 61.6%  | 59.2%  | 59.6%  | 60.1 ± 1.3%  |\\n| 64  | 50%     | 61.6%  | 60.0%  | 64.4%  | 62.0 ± 2.3%  |\\n| 96  | 25%     | 52.6%  | 58.2%  | 52.8%  | 54.5 ± 3.2%  |\\n| 128 | 0%      | 59.8%  | 54.0%  | 60.2%  | 58.0 ± 3.5%  |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"已完成。M-curve flat是VTR on pixel-shuffle的核心发现： re-encoding而非compression是因果因子。任何压缩比下均near-lossless。\\n\\n\\n数据已全部在registry中确认。M=16 (56.9±1.3%) ≈ M=128 (58.0±3.5%)， 差异<1.1pp。M-curve flatness是confirmed fact (D105)。 M=128 seed43的54.0%是该seed下特定task表现偏弱导致（cream_cheese 32.2%, ketchup 34.8%均显著低于其他seed），但不影响核心结论。 所有5个M值的3-seed mean均在baseline ~59%的±5pp内。 此plan_id实质已完成，无需预测。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTR M=128 全量 (已confirmed negative)\",\n    \"description\": \"VTR (cross-attention compressor + decoder) M=128在OpenVLA上20K步评估。 已确认0% SR——严重过拟合，模型每步输出identical action。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_vtr_m128_sr\": 0,\n      \"episodes_evaluated\": 44,\n      \"failure_mode\": \"identical action every timestep\",\n      \"overfitting_severity\": \"complete — model collapsed to single-action policy\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"已完成。0% SR将作为Claim 4 negative evidence呈现： \\\"VTR ceiling depends on connector type — pixel-shuffle benefits enormously (0%→60%+) while MLP projector suffers (74%→0%).\\\"\\n\\n\\nMLP projector的3层GELU已将SigLIP patch embeddings投射为LLM-ready tokens， 每个token独立承载语义（CV=0.215，moderate heterogeneity但无空间纠缠）。 VTR的cross-attention将256个独立token强制经过bottleneck再decode， 这对已经独立的tokens是destructive operation：(1) 引入了不必要的信息混合， (2) 22M额外参数在LIBERO的小规模数据（~50 demo/task）上快速过拟合， (3) 20K步已足够让compressor学会\\\"记住\\\"训练分布而非泛化。 对比SmolVLA：pixel-shuffle tokens确实需要re-encoding来解空间纠缠， 所以同样的VTR在那里成功（0%→60%+）。 此failure本身是median档叙事的核心evidence。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC-only M=32 (75%压缩)\",\n    \"description\": \"仅cross-attention compressor（无decoder），M=32，在OpenVLA上训练。 测试VTC-only是否能避免full VTR M=128的过拟合。 当前状态：train_openvla_sc_m32_vtconly_seed42 RUNNING。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_vtconly_m32_sr\": 7,\n      \"openvla_vtconly_m32_sr_range\": [\n        0,\n        15\n      ],\n      \"openvla_vtconly_m32_failure_mode\": \"severe degradation, possible partial overfitting\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC-only M-sweep predicted results\",\n        \"data\": \"| M   | 压缩率  | 预测SR     | 预测区间     | vs Baseline 74% |\\n|-----|---------|-----------|------------|----------------|\\n| 32  | 75%     | ~7%       | [0%, 15%]  | -91% relative  |\\n| 64  | 50%     | ~4%       | [0%, 15%]  | -95% relative  |\\n| 96  | 62.5%保留| ~2%       | [0%, 10%]  | -97% relative  |\\n| 128 | 0% (VTR)| 0%        | confirmed  | -100%          |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"M=32的strong compression理论上是最有可能\\\"accidentally work\\\"的配置： (1) 参数最少→过拟合风险最低，(2) 信息压缩最极端→如果某些token确实冗余 则可能保留核心信息。但MLP projector的CV=0.215意味着tokens间heterogeneity 不够极端（不像SmolVLA CV=0.314的空间纠缠），没有\\\"需要被解开的结构\\\" 供cross-attention利用。预测SR<15%。\\n\\n\\n核心问题未变：MLP projector tokens不需要re-encoding。VTC-only去掉了decoder （减少约11M参数），但cross-attention compressor仍将256个token压缩到32个query。 这对MLP projector是根本性错误——每个original token独立承载语义， cross-attention将8个token的信息挤进1个query（256/32=8:1）， 不同于pixel-shuffle tokens中spatial信息可通过re-encoding恢复。 M=32的强压缩可能提供些许regularization（相比M=128）， 所以过拟合可能没那么complete，但SR仍将极低。 少数\\\"简单\\\"task可能偶尔成功（如chocolate_pudding在OpenVLA baseline中>80%）， 但overall SR远低于baseline 74%。预测0-15%，中位数~7%。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC-only M=64 (50%压缩)\",\n    \"description\": \"VTC-only M=64在OpenVLA上训练。 当前状态：train_openvla_sc_m64_seed42_v3 RUNNING。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_vtconly_m64_sr\": 4,\n      \"openvla_vtconly_m64_sr_range\": [\n        0,\n        15\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"M=64结果与M=32共同形成OpenVLA VTC-only M-sweep。 无论具体数值排序如何（M=32 > M=64 or M=32 < M=64）， 只要全部<15%就确认VTR/VTC对MLP projector无效。\\n\\n\\nM=64保留50%的token数。M=128 full VTR已0%，M=64 VTC-only减少了decoder 但仍有cross-attention bottleneck。比M=32的regularization弱（更多参数自由度）， 比M=128少了decoder。如果过拟合是dominant failure mode（M=128 evidence支持此判断）， M=64介于M=32和M=128之间，可能比M=32稍差。 但如果压缩损失是dominant failure mode，M=64应比M=32好（保留更多信息）。 在median档下，过拟合是主因→M=64可能≤M=32。预测~4%，区间[0, 15%]。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC-only M=96 (25%压缩)\",\n    \"description\": \"VTC-only M=96在OpenVLA上训练。最接近passthrough（96/256=37.5%保留）。 当前状态：train_openvla_sc_m96_seed42_v3 RUNNING。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_vtconly_m96_sr\": 2,\n      \"openvla_vtconly_m96_sr_range\": [\n        0,\n        10\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"三个M值形成的M-sweep pattern本身是informative的： 如果SmolVLA M-curve flat而OpenVLA M-curve monotonically decreasing（或all near 0%）， 这两条曲线的对比就是一张figure。\\n\\n\\nM=96 VTC-only最接近M=128的configuration——压缩比最低，参数自由度最大。 M=128 full VTR的0%主要由过拟合导致，M=96 VTC-only虽去掉decoder但 compressor参数仍然很多（96个query × hidden_dim）。 在三个M值中最容易过拟合，预测为最差。~2%，区间[0, 10%]。 若M=96≈0%且M=32~7%，则形成inverse M-curve（越大的M越差）， 与SmolVLA的flat M-curve形成sharp contrast——进一步支持 \\\"VTR的行为本身取决于connector type\\\"的论点。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.95 (5% removal)\",\n    \"description\": \"L2 norm importance-based pruning k=0.95在OpenVLA上。 统一pruning method与X-VLA（两者均L2 norm）。 对比：random pruning k=0.95 = 69.4%。 当前状态：eval_openvla_prune_l2norm_k095 RUNNING。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_l2norm_k095_sr\": 70,\n      \"openvla_l2norm_k095_sr_range\": [\n        59,\n        79\n      ],\n      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": \"+0.6\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"k=0.95是两种方法差异最小的数据点。 用于完善L2 norm全曲线，与random曲线overlay展示method invariance。\\n\\n\\nk=0.95仅移除13/256 = 5%的token。在如此低的removal ratio下， importance-based (L2 norm) vs random的差异被两个因素压缩到极小： (1) 被移除的13个token中，L2 norm选中的\\\"最不重要\\\"vs随机选中的差异有限—— MLP projector CV=0.215意味着importance分布的tail不极端； (2) 500 episodes的statistical power在1-2pp的difference下不足以detect。 Random=69.4%。L2 norm预测~70%（可能69-72%），差异在统计噪声内。 核心论点不受影响：无论pruning method，MLP projector在k=0.95保持>90%性能。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.9 (10% removal)\",\n    \"description\": \"L2 norm k=0.9在OpenVLA上。对比random k=0.9 = 62.0%。 当前状态：eval_openvla_prune_l2norm_k09 RUNNING。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_l2norm_k09_sr\": 63,\n      \"openvla_l2norm_k09_sr_range\": [\n        52,\n        72\n      ],\n      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": \"+1\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-model L2 norm k=0.9对比\",\n        \"data\": \"| Model   | Connector       | CV    | L2 norm k=0.9 SR | 对比baseline |\\n|---------|-----------------|-------|------------------|-------------|\\n| π0      | Pure linear     | 0.038 | ~99% (offline)   | -0.7%       |\\n| X-VLA   | Linear+BART 12L | 0.151 | 97.6%            | -1.6pp      |\\n| OpenVLA | 3-layer MLP     | 0.215 | ~63%             | -15% rel    |\\n| SmolVLA | Pixel-shuffle   | 0.314 | 0%               | -100%       |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"k=0.9是论文中cross-model comparison的关键k值： 所有4个model在同一pruning method下的对比清晰展示taxonomy。 L2 norm unified protocol使得cross-model comparison methodologically clean。\\n\\n\\nk=0.9移除26/256 = 10%的token。L2 norm有一点点空间选择性保留重要token， 但26个token中importance ranking的真正差异仍然有限。 Random=62%。L2 norm可能有marginal improvement to ~63%（1pp）， 但也可能恰好worse by 1-2pp due to sampling variance。 重要的是：62%±5pp，仍在\\\"graded degradation\\\"的范畴内， 与X-VLA k=0.9 (97.6%, robust) 形成stark contrast—— OpenVLA在10% removal就已经-16% relative，X-VLA还几乎无损。 这直接isolate connector effect：same pruning method, same k, different degradation pattern。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.7 (30% removal)\",\n    \"description\": \"L2 norm k=0.7。对比random k=0.7 = 49.0%。 此k值是X-VLA cliff point (56.2%)的对照。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_l2norm_k07_sr\": 51,\n      \"openvla_l2norm_k07_sr_range\": [\n        42,\n        58\n      ],\n      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": \"+2\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OpenVLA k=0.7 L2 norm是统一protocol下最重要的cross-model对比点之一。 与X-VLA同k同method但degradation pattern截然不同，直接isolate connector effect。\\n\\n\\nk=0.7移除30%的token。L2 norm的importance-based selection在较大removal ratio下 有更多空间发挥——30%中最不重要的token确实可以被识别。 但OpenVLA CV=0.215意味着importance分布不极端（不像SmolVLA CV=0.314）， L2 norm vs random的差距仍然modest。 Random=49%，L2 norm预测~51%（+2pp），区间[42, 58]。 关键cross-model对比：OpenVLA L2 norm k=0.7 ~51% vs X-VLA L2 norm k=0.7 = 56.2%。 两者数值接近但模式不同——OpenVLA是smooth curve上的一点（k=0.9: 63% → k=0.7: 51%, delta=-12pp），X-VLA是cliff-edge（k=0.9: 97.6% → k=0.7: 56.2%, delta=-41pp）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.5 (50% removal)\",\n    \"description\": \"L2 norm k=0.5。对比random k=0.5 = 37.4%。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_l2norm_k05_sr\": 40,\n      \"openvla_l2norm_k05_sr_range\": [\n        30,\n        47\n      ],\n      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": \"+3\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"50% removal下L2 norm的优势最可能visible——保留最重要的一半token。 MLP projector的CV=0.215意味着top-50% vs random-50%在信息量上有 measurable但不dramatic的差异。Random=37.4%，L2 norm预测~40%（+3pp）。 +3pp是500 episodes下可detect的差异（Wilson CI width ~±4pp）， 但单次实验不一定statistically significant。 即使L2 norm优势达到+5pp (42%)，仍然是severe degradation vs baseline 74%， taxonomy classification不变（smooth graded）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.3 (70% removal)\",\n    \"description\": \"L2 norm k=0.3。对比random k=0.3 = 20.6%。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_l2norm_k03_sr\": 23,\n      \"openvla_l2norm_k03_sr_range\": [\n        15,\n        30\n      ],\n      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": \"+2\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2 norm vs Random完整对比（含预测）\",\n        \"data\": \"| k    | Random SR | L2-norm SR | Delta  | 解读                        |\\n|------|-----------|------------|--------|-----------------------------|\\n| 1.0  | 74.0%     | 74.0%      | 0      | baseline, 无pruning          |\\n| 0.95 | 69.4%     | ~70%       | ~+0.6  | 差异在noise内                |\\n| 0.9  | 62.0%     | ~63%       | ~+1    | marginal L2 advantage        |\\n| 0.7  | 49.0%     | ~51%       | ~+2    | visible但modest advantage    |\\n| 0.5  | 37.4%     | ~40%       | ~+3    | L2 advantage最大点           |\\n| 0.3  | 20.6%     | ~23%       | ~+2    | extreme removal, 优势缩小    |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"L2 norm全曲线确认：OpenVLA graded degradation与pruning方法无关。 两条曲线的near-overlap是taxonomy robustness的直接evidence。 论文可一句话总结：\\\"L2-norm和random pruning在OpenVLA上产生near-identical degradation curves (Δ<3pp across all k), confirming that connector type — not pruning strategy — determines pruning tolerance.\\\"\\n\\n\\n70% removal是extreme。L2 norm在此能保留最关键的30%， 但绝对信息损失已很大。Random=20.6%，L2 norm预测~23%。 在此极端条件下，L2 norm的marginal advantage开始diminish—— 即使保留了最重要的30%，remaining 30%中也有很多重要token被丢弃。 两种方法都在20-25%区间内挣扎。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"X-VLA L2-norm pruning k=0.7 seed44 (cliff variance)\",\n    \"description\": \"X-VLA k=0.7使用seed44重复。验证cliff位置的seed robustness。 Seed42 = 56.2%。当前状态：eval_xvla_prune_k07_seed44 RUNNING。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"xvla_k07_seed44_sr\": 52,\n      \"xvla_k07_seed44_sr_range\": [\n        40,\n        70\n      ],\n      \"cliff_pattern_preserved\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"X-VLA cliff-point seed variance\",\n        \"data\": \"| k    | Seed42  | Seed44 (pred) | 2-seed Mean | Interpretation          |\\n|------|---------|---------------|-------------|-------------------------|\\n| 1.0  | 99.2%   | ~99%          | ~99%        | baseline stable         |\\n| 0.95 | 99.0%   | ~98%          | ~98.5%      | robust region           |\\n| 0.9  | 97.6%   | ~96.5%        | ~97%        | robust region           |\\n| 0.7  | 56.2%   | ~52%          | ~54%        | CLIFF — high variance   |\\n| 0.5  | 42.6%   | ~40%          | ~41%        | below cliff, stabilizes |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cliff variance是expected phenomenon（不是noise），可以直接在论文中讨论： \\\"cliff位置在k~0.7处，但exact SR在不同seed下波动±10pp， reflecting the stochastic nature of dependency breaking when token removal crosses the critical threshold.\\\" 若seed44 < 45%，cliff比seed42更sharp → 更强的evidence； 若seed44 > 60%，cliff更shallow → 仍然是>30pp drop from k=0.9。\\n\\n\\nk=0.7是X-VLA的cliff point——从k=0.9的97.6%骤降到56.2% (seed42)。 Cliff points天然high-variance，原因是： (1) BART encoder的12层transformer mixing创建了partial token dependencies， 在k=0.7恰好跨过dependencies被破坏的threshold； (2) seed决定eval episodes的随机初始状态和token removal order， cliff附近某些task的成功高度依赖于具体哪些token被保留； (3) Seed42的per-task分析：task1=2%, task4=28%, task6=12%, task8=0% vs task0=94%, task2=100%——bimodality极端。 seed44的specific task分布会不同，可能某些在seed42失败的task反而成功， 反之亦然。预测overall 40-70%，中位数~52%。 无论具体数值，只要k=0.9 >> k=0.7（>30pp gap），cliff pattern就成立。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"X-VLA L2-norm pruning k=0.9 seed44 (robust region)\",\n    \"description\": \"X-VLA k=0.9 seed44。Seed42 = 97.6%。验证robust region稳定性。 当前状态：eval_xvla_prune_k09_seed44 RUNNING。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"xvla_k09_seed44_sr\": 96.5,\n      \"xvla_k09_seed44_sr_range\": [\n        94,\n        99\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"k=0.9 seed44的高SR（>94%）与k=0.7 seed44的cliff（~52%） 共同确认threshold-graded pattern的定性stability。 2-seed evidence足以支持论文claim（加上per-task breakdown更convincing）。\\n\\n\\nk=0.9在robust region内（cliff在k=0.7）。仅移除10% token。 BART encoder的partial dependencies在此ratio下未被破坏—— 50个token中移除5个，保留的45个token仍足以覆盖绝大多数spatial和semantic信息。 Seed variance在robust region天然很小：不同seed改变的是\\\"哪5个token被移除\\\"， 但L2 norm保证移除的是importance最低的5个，这些token在所有seed下都是 relatively dispensable的。Seed42=97.6%，seed44预测~96.5%（可能95-99%）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.7 seed43\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.7 seed43重复。Seed42 = 49.0%。 当前状态：eval_openvla_prune_random_k07_seed43_v2 RUNNING。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_random_k07_seed43_sr\": 47,\n      \"openvla_random_k07_seed43_sr_range\": [\n        40,\n        56\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Seed43的一致性确认OpenVLA smooth degradation的reproducibility。 与X-VLA k=0.7的high seed variance形成对比—— \\\"smooth degradation is reproducible, cliff is stochastic.\\\"\\n\\n\\nOpenVLA k=0.7在smooth degradation curve上（不是cliff point）， seed variance应显著低于X-VLA k=0.7。MLP projector的partial independence 意味着不同random mask导致的信息损失是relatively consistent的—— 没有特定token的移除会cause catastrophic failure（不像X-VLA的critical tokens）。 500 episodes × 10 tasks提供了good statistical power。 Seed42=49%，seed43预测47%（±5pp）。 如果delta<3pp，则single-seed结果高度representative。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.5 seed43\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.5 seed43。Seed42 = 37.4%。 当前状态：eval_openvla_prune_random_k05_seed43_v2 RUNNING。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_random_k05_seed43_sr\": 36,\n      \"openvla_random_k05_seed43_sr_range\": [\n        30,\n        44\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"同k=0.7的推理。k=0.5移除50%，random mask的具体配置差异更大， 所以seed variance可能比k=0.7稍高（±4pp vs ±3pp）。 但MLP projector的graded特性保证不会出现cliff-like discontinuity。 Seed42=37.4%，seed43预测~36%。若在33-41%范围内均合理。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RoboFlamingo Perceiver Resampler baseline + pruning sweep\",\n    \"description\": \"在LIBERO上fine-tune RoboFlamingo (Perceiver Resampler connector)， 然后执行pruning sweep。验证第4种connector family的pruning行为。 状态：planned，未开始。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"will_complete_before_deadline\": false,\n      \"baseline_sr_if_run\": 45,\n      \"baseline_sr_range\": [\n        35,\n        55\n      ],\n      \"perceiver_cv_prediction\": 0.15,\n      \"perceiver_cv_range\": [\n        0.1,\n        0.2\n      ],\n      \"pruning_k09_sr_if_run\": 40,\n      \"pruning_k07_sr_if_run\": 25,\n      \"pruning_behavior\": \"moderate graded, possibly with soft threshold\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"完整taxonomy预测（含Perceiver Resampler）\",\n        \"data\": \"| Connector         | Model         | CV    | k=0.9 SR | k=0.7 SR | Pattern         | Status    |\\n|-------------------|---------------|-------|----------|----------|-----------------|-----------|\\n| Pure linear       | π0 3.3B       | 0.038 | ~99%     | ~99%     | Immune          | Confirmed |\\n| Linear+BART 12L   | X-VLA 880M    | 0.151 | 97.6%    | 56.2%    | Threshold-graded| Confirmed |\\n| Perceiver Resamp. | RoboFlamingo  | ~0.15 | ~40%?    | ~25%?    | Soft graded?    | Predicted |\\n| 3-layer MLP       | OpenVLA 7B    | 0.215 | 62%      | 49%      | Smooth graded   | Confirmed |\\n| Pixel-shuffle 16× | SmolVLA 450M  | 0.314 | 0%       | 0%       | Catastrophic    | Confirmed |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"在median档下，RoboFlamingo不会完成。论文以5模型×3 connector families提交。 Perceiver Resampler作为Discussion section的future work： \\\"Our taxonomy and CV diagnostic predict Perceiver Resampler (used in Flamingo) would show intermediate behavior (CV~0.15); validation is left to future work.\\\" 这是acceptable的——4 confirmed connector types + 5 models已是 most comprehensive cross-architecture VLA token analysis。 Reviewer可能要求但可以argue coverage已足够。 如果reviewer要求且有revision opportunity，可作为revision deliverable。\\n\\nPerceiver Resampler使用learnable query tokens通过cross-attention从encoder output中提取固定数量的compressed representations。架构上与VTC类似 （都是cross-attention压缩），但位于connector（而非compression module）。 预测CV=0.10-0.20（between π0=0.038 and OpenVLA=0.215）： (1) cross-attention引入了soft inter-token dependencies（类似BART）， (2) 但每个query token attend to all encoder tokens（global receptive field）， 信息分布比MLP projector更structured但比pixel-shuffle less entangled。 pruning行为预测：moderate graded degradation，可能在k~0.8有soft threshold （类似X-VLA但更gentle）——Perceiver的global attention给每个token 提供了more redundancy than MLP but less than pure linear。\\n但此实验需要至少3-5天：(1) RoboFlamingo codebase adaptation (~1天), (2) LIBERO data loading + fine-tuning pipeline (~0.5天 setup + 1天 training), (3) pruning sweep + evaluation (~1天), (4) analysis (~0.5天)。 距离abstract deadline (May 26) 仅6天，距离paper deadline (May 29) 仅9天。 无法在deadline前完成。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":268,"startLine":1,"totalLines":268}}}
